hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","1 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Dhi Iswan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Ummah is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter, and when the Day of Resurrection comes, every Muslim man will be given a man from among the People of the Two Books, and it will be said: O Muslim, this is your ransom from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Sa'id ibn Yazid, and no one narrated it from Sa'id ibn Yazid except Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi."
"2","2 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Humrah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, that Abu Mijlaz informed him, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Musa, that two men disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a camel, each of them claiming it was his, and with each one of them came two witnesses testifying that the camel was his, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that it be divided between them in halves. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, except al-Dahhak; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it."
"3","3 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata and Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not marry women except to suitable matches, and none shall marry them off except the guardians, and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except al-Hajjaj; Mubashshir ibn Ubayd is alone in narrating it."
"4","4 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khumayr al-Rahabi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no one except that I will recognize him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And how will you recognize them, O Messenger of Allah, among the multitude of creatures? He said: What do you think, if you entered an enclosure in which there were dark black horses, and among them a horse with a white blaze and white feet, would you not recognize it among them? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then my Ummah on that day will be radiant with white marks from ablution."
"5","5 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ufayr ibn Mi'dan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah twice - and he was blind - leading the people in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ufayr; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it."
"6","6 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ufayr ibn Mi'dan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The jinn were directed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twice, and the nobles of the jinn were at Nasibin. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ufayr; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it."
"7","7 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ufayr narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to me, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Jibril comes to me in the form of Dihyah al-Kalbi. Anas said: And Dihyah was a large, handsome, fair man. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ufayr; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it."
"8","8 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When I was taken up in the night journey, I passed by people who had nails of copper with which they scratched their faces and chests, so I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are those who eat the flesh of people and attack their honor. No one narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr except Safwan; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it."
"9","9 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim. No one narrated it from Muhammad except Kathir, and no one narrated it from Kathir except Hafs ibn Sulayman."
"10","10 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man from among his Companions who had a pain - and I was with him - so he took his hand and placed his hand upon his forehead - and he used to consider that part of the complete visiting of the sick - and he said: Indeed Allah said: My fire, I unleash it upon My believing servant, so that it may be his share of the Fire in the Hereafter. No one narrated it from Abu Salih, and he is al-Ash'ari, except Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah; Abd al-Rahman is alone in narrating it."
"11","11 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq, from Awsat al-Bajali, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after it, two before Asr, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq, from Awsat al-Bajali, except Ismail ibn Ayyash. And al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Aws, from Anbasah."
"12","12 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave us in confusion regarding our religion; he forbade us from blowing into drink."
"13","13 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, from Wail ibn Dawud, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you swear an oath, then see that something else is better, do that which is better and expiate for your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Wail ibn Dawud except Khalid ibn Yazid; al-Hawti is alone in narrating it."
"14","14 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Musa al-Lahuni narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it without asking you will be helped in it, and if you are given it after asking you will be left to it; and if you swear an oath, then see something else better than it, do that which is better and expiate for your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid except Yazid; Abd al-Aziz is alone in narrating it."
"15","15 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from Urfutah, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it. No one narrated this hadith from Urfutah except al-Walid ibn Abbad, and no one narrated it from al-Walid except Ismail ibn Ayyash; Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak is alone in narrating it."
"16","16 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Artah ibn al-Mundhir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands at the takbir for bowing, and at the takbir when going down in prostration. No one narrated this hadith from Artah except al-Jarrah."
"17","17 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Abu Mahdi Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Umm al-Sha'tha narrated to me, from Umm Ismah al-Awsiyyah, a woman from Qays, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who commits a sin except that the angel entrusted with recording his sins pauses for three hours; if he seeks Allah's forgiveness for that sin of his during any of those hours, it will not be held against him on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Ismah except with this chain; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it."
"18","18 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu Wahb Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kala'i, from Makhul, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he traced a hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever among you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Abu Wahb, and no one narrated it from Abu Wahb except Suwayd; al-Hawti is alone in narrating it."
"19","19 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to me, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came in the morning to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, and he said: What brought you in the morning, O Zirr? I said: I seek knowledge. He said: Come in the morning as a scholar or a learner, and do not go beyond that. For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no Muslim servant who seeks knowledge except that the angels lay down their wings for him out of pleasure with what he does. He said: Then I asked him about wiping over the socks, and I said: I find some unease about that within myself. He said: When we were traveling with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we were commanded not to take off our socks for three nights and their days, except from major impurity, but for stool, urine, and sleep. And for the resident, a day and a night. No one narrated it from Hafs ibn Sulayman except Ali ibn Ayyash."
"20","20 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Chastity is of two kinds: chastity of continence and chastity of marriage. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Mubashshir ibn Ubayd."
"21","21 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah al-A'ma, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he came to Ibn Abbas and said: O Ibn Abbas, how long you have led people astray. He said: And what is that, O Urayyah? He said: A man goes out in ihram for Hajj or Umrah, and when he performs tawaf, you claim that he has become released from ihram, yet Abu Bakr and Umar used to forbid that. He said: Woe to you, are they more worthy in your view, or what is in the Book of Allah and what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established among his Companions and his Ummah? Urwah said: They both knew the Book of Allah and what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established better than me and you. Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: So Urwah silenced him in argument."
"22","22 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Abu Adhabah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Adhabah except al-Jarrah; al-Hawti is alone in narrating it."
"23","23 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who fasts without her husband's permission, then he desires something from her and she refuses him, Allah records three major sins against her. No one narrated it from al-Awza'i except Baqiyyah; al-Hawti is alone in narrating it."
"24","24 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three supplications are answered, with no doubt in them: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of a parent against his child, and the supplication of the traveler. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, except al-Awza'i; Abu al-Mughirah is alone in narrating it, and the narration of the people is: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ja'far."
"25","25 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A report is not like eyewitnessing; for Allah the Exalted informed Musa ibn Imran about what his people did after him, and he did not cast down the Tablets, but when he witnessed that, he cast down the Tablets."
"26","26 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Abu al-Mughirah."
"27","27 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared Safiyyah free of pregnancy by one menstrual cycle. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in narrating it."
"28","28 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya al-Atrabulsi narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Marwan, from Yazid Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take a midday nap, for Satan does not take a midday nap. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Kathir, and no one narrated it from Kathir except Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya; Ali ibn Ayyash is alone in narrating it."
"29","29 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from Urfutah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does a kindness to you, repay him; if you are unable to repay him, supplicate for him until he knows that you have thanked him, for Allah is Appreciative and loves the thankful. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Urfutah; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in narrating it, from al-Walid ibn Abbad."
"30","30 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever keeps a dog, his deeds decrease every day by a qirat. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam."
"31","31 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take the mosques as pathways, except for remembrance or prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri, whose name is Huyayy ibn Hani, and no one narrated it from Abu Qabil except Ali ibn Hawshab; Yahya ibn Salih is alone in narrating it."
"32","32 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Uqbah ibn Ruman narrated to me, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever removes from the path of the Muslims something that harms them, Allah records for him a good deed thereby, and whoever has a good deed recorded for him with Him, He will admit him to Paradise thereby. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam is alone in narrating it."
"33","33 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Artah ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ruzayq, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Abu al-Darda, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not eat reclining, and do not step over the necks of people on Friday. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Artah ibn al-Mundhir is alone in narrating it."
"34","34 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ata narrated to us, from Maslamah ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani, from his uncle Abu Mashja'ah, from Abu al-Darda, he said: They mentioned kinship ties before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said: Whoever maintains his kinship ties, his term of life is extended. He said: His lifespan is not increased; Allah the Exalted said: When their term comes, they cannot delay it an hour nor advance it. But it is a man who has righteous offspring, and they supplicate for him after him, and that reaches him; that is what extends his term. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Ata is alone in narrating it."
"35","35 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: al-Mahdi led us in prayer and recited aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. So I spoke to him about that, and he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."
"36","36 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: al-Mahdi wrote to me appointing me to office, and ordered me to be firm in judgment, and said in his letter: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: By My might and majesty, I will surely take revenge against the oppressor in this world and the next, and I will surely take revenge against one who saw an oppressed person and was able to help him, but did not do so. These two hadiths are not narrated from al-Mahdi except with this chain; Yahya ibn Hamzah is alone in narrating them."
"37","37 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Abu Amr al-Awza'i narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you has a servant who has spared him hardship, let him feed him; if he does not do so, let him hand him a morsel. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Yahya ibn Hamzah; his son is alone in narrating it from him."
"38","38 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Dawud ibn Isa al-Kufi narrated to me, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, he said: Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated to me. He said: My father narrated to me, that his father sent him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need. He said: I found him sitting with his Companions in the mosque, and I could not speak to him. When he prayed Maghrib, he stood praying voluntarily until the muezzin called for Isha prayer and the people gathered, then he prayed the prayer, then he stood praying voluntarily until those who remained in the mosque left, then he went to his house and I followed him. When he heard me he said: Who is this? And he turned to me, and I said: Ibn Abbas. He said: The cousin of the Messenger of Allah? I said: The cousin of the Messenger of Allah. He said: Welcome to the cousin of the Messenger of Allah; what brought you? I said: My father sent me for such-and-such. He said: Did you just come now? I said: No. He said: Since you did not leave until this hour of yours, you shall not leave. So he entered his house and I entered with him. I said: I shall surely observe the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tonight. So he slept until I heard his snoring, then he woke and cast his gaze to the sky and recited these verses in Surah Al Imran: Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth, the five verses, until he reached: Indeed, You do not break the promise. Then he said: O Allah, place light in my hearing, light in my sight, light above me, light beneath me, light on my right, light on my left, and grant me light with You. And beside him was a washbasin of brass with a siwak placed upon it, so he cleaned his teeth, then performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs, then returned and slept again until I heard his snoring, then he woke and recited the verses and supplicated with the supplication, then cleaned his teeth, then performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs, then slept until I heard his snoring, then he woke and recited the verses, then supplicated with the supplication, then cleaned his teeth, then performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs, then slept until I heard his snoring, then he woke and recited the verses and supplicated with the supplication, then cleaned his teeth, then performed ablution, then prayed a prayer in which I recognized that he was performing witr, then he said: Has the boy slept? I said: No. So I stood and performed ablution, then I came and went to his left side, so he took my ears with his fingers and turned me until he placed me at his right side, then he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, then he went out to prayer."
"39","39 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from Urfutah, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Alqamah ibn Qays, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Five verses have passed and five remain: the splitting of the moon has passed, and we saw it; the smoke has passed; the great assault has passed; and the Romans have passed."
"40","40 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Actions are only by intentions, and every person shall have only what he intended; so whoever's migration was to Allah and His Messenger, his migration is to Allah and His Messenger, and whoever's migration was for a worldly gain he attains or a woman he marries, his migration is to that to which he migrated. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Yahya ibn Hamzah, Abu Khulayd Utbah ibn Hammad, and al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"41","41 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, he said: Abu Rafi narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Friday, except in days before it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"42","42 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awza'i narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: My father Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have feared that I have perished. He said: Why? I said: Allah forbade a person to be praised for what he did not do, and I find that I love praise; Allah forbade arrogance, and I find that I love beauty; and Allah forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you not pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise praised? He said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. So he lived praised, and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylimah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Yahya ibn Hamzah; his son is alone in narrating it from him."
"43","43 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awza'i, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tarif claimed, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night the company of jinn were directed to him, when a man from among the jinn came with a flame of fire toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Jibril said: O Muhammad, shall I not teach you words which, when you say them, his flame will be extinguished and he will fall upon his nostril? Say: I seek refuge in the noble Face of Allah, and in the perfect words of Allah which no righteous one nor wicked one can go beyond, from the evil of what descends from the heaven and what ascends therein, and from the evil of what He created in the earth and what comes out of it, and from the evil of the trials of night and day, and from the evil of the visitors of night and day, except a visitor who comes with good, O Most Merciful. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Yahya ibn Hamzah; his son is alone in narrating it from him."
"44","44 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Amr ibn al-As, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Eloquent speech, all of eloquence, is a branch of Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"45","45 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aidh narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Uthman al-Awqas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will continue to fight the disbelievers until you fight a people small of eye, flat of nose, as if their faces were hammered shields. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abu Uthman al-Awqas; al-Walid is alone in narrating it."
"46","46 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Maslamah ibn Amr al-Qadi narrated to me, he said: I found in the register of al-Zuhri in his handwriting, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever among you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. This hadith is not narrated from al-Zuhri except with this chain."
"47","47 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Abu Salih al-Khawlani, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will always remain a group from my Ummah fighting at the gates of Damascus and around it, and at the gates of Bayt al-Maqdis and around it; the forsaking of those who forsake them will not harm them, manifest until the Hour comes. No one narrated it from Amir al-Ahwal except al-Walid ibn Abbad; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in narrating it."
"48","48 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated it from al-Nu'man except Yahya."
"49","49 - And from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"50","50 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Dinar, that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling wala and giving it as a gift. No one narrated it from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, except Yahya ibn Hamzah; his son is alone in narrating it from him, and the people narrated it from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar."
"51","51 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to me, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir narrating from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. Aishah said: Then what about private parts? He said: For every person among them on that day is a matter that occupies him. No one entered between al-Zuhri and al-Zubaydi, among those who narrated this hadith from al-Zubaydi, al-Nu'man except Yahya ibn Hamzah; his son is alone in narrating it from him."
"52","52 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught a man to say when he lies down to sleep: O Allah, I have turned my face to You, leaned my back upon You, entrusted my affair to You, and submitted my soul to You, in fear and hope of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent. If he dies that night, he will be forgiven. No one narrated it from Amr ibn Qays except Thawr ibn Yazid, and no one narrated it from Thawr except Yahya ibn Hamzah; his son is alone in narrating it from him."
"53","53 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield from the Fire. No one narrated it from al-Awza'i except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"54","54 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make Your grip severe upon Mudar, and make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf. No one narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr, except Shu'ayb."
"55","55 - Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray. Thus Abu Zayd narrated to us this hadith with a connected chain, from Abd Allah ibn Amr. Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention in the chain: Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"56","56 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Yazid Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Abu al-Mughirah."
"57","57 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You and your wealth belong to your father."
"58","58 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim Abu Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father Abd Allah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a tent of leather of his, so I greeted him, then I said: May I enter? He said: Enter. So I put my head in, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution thoroughly. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I enter entirely? He said: Entirely. When I entered, he said to me: Count six traits before the Hour: the death of your Prophet - Awf said: I was struck with grief thereby such as I never was - he said: Say: One. I said: One. He said: And the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, and a trial that will be among you, encompassing the houses of the Arabs, and a disease that will seize you like the throat-disease of sheep, and wealth will become abundant among you, until a man will be given one hundred dinars yet remain dissatisfied, and a truce that will be between you and Banu al-Asfar, then they will betray, and come to you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand. No one narrated it from Makhul except Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr."
"59","59 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Malik ibn Yukhamir al-Saksaki, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Migration is of two kinds: one is that you abandon evil deeds, and the other is that you migrate to Allah and His Messenger; and migration does not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance continues to be accepted until the sun rises from the west; when it rises, every heart will be sealed with what is in it, and people will be spared deeds. It is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf except from this route."
"60","60 - Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Busri al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aidh al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Tarfah Abbad ibn al-Rayyan al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: I heard Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi say: Amir ibn Ludayn al-Ash'ari narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Layla al-Ash'ari say: Abu Dharr narrated to me, he said: The first thing that called me to Islam was that we were an Arab people, and a year of drought struck us, so I carried my mother and my brother - his name was Unays - to in-laws of ours in upper Najd. When we settled with them they honored us, but when a man of the tribe saw that, he went to my maternal uncle and said: Do you know that Unays visits your wife in your absence? It struck his heart, so I returned from herding my camels and found him gloomy, weeping. I said: Why do you weep, O uncle? He told me the news. I said: May Allah forbid that; we abhor indecency, even though the times have afflicted us, and you have spoiled for us the goodness with which you began; there is no way to stay together. So I carried my mother and my brother until we settled near Makkah. My brother said: I will contend with a man over water in poetry - and he was a poet - so I said: Do not do it. But stubbornness drove him until he contended with Durayd ibn al-Simmah, matching his herd against his herd. By Allah, Durayd on that day was more poetic than my brother, so they sought judgment from al-Khansa, and she ruled for my brother against Durayd, because Durayd had proposed to her to her father, and she said: An old man; I have no need of him, so she held that against him. So we joined his herd to ours, and we had a large herd. Then I came to Makkah and began at al-Safa, where there were men of Quraysh, and it had reached me that among them was a Sabian, or madman, or poet, or magician. I said: Where is this one you claim? They said: He is there where you see. I turned toward him, and by Allah, I had not gone past them the distance of a stone's throw before they fell upon me with every bone, stone, and clod, and covered me in my blood. So I came to the House and entered between the curtains and the building, and stayed there thirty days, eating and drinking nothing except Zamzam water, until on a bright moonlit night, two women from Khuza'ah came and circumambulated the House, then mentioned Isaf and Nailah - two idols they used to worship - so I stuck my head out from under the curtains and said: Load one of them upon the other. They became angry, then said: By Allah, if our men were present you would not have spoken thus. So I went out following their tracks until they met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Who are you two? From whom are you? From where have you come? And what brought you? They told him the news. He said: Where did you leave the Sabian? They said: We left him between the curtains and the building. He said to them: Did he say anything to you? They said: Yes, a word that fills the mouth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then they slipped away, and I came forward until I reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I greeted him at that moment. He said: Who are you? From whom are you? From where are you? From where have you come? And what brought you? So I began to tell him the news. He said: From where did you eat and drink? I said: From Zamzam water. He said: It is indeed nourishing food. And with him was Abu Bakr, who said: O Messenger of Allah, allow me to give him dinner. He said: Yes. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out walking, and Abu Bakr took my hand until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at the door of Abu Bakr, then Abu Bakr entered his house. Then he brought some raisins from the raisins of Taif, and began to throw them to us handful by handful, and we ate from them until we were full. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service. He said: A land has been shown to me, a land of palm trees; I think it is none but Tihamah, so go out to your people and call them to what you have entered. He said: So I went out until I came to my mother and my brother, and told them the news, and they said: We have no aversion to the religion you entered, so we accepted Islam. Then we went out until we came to Madinah, and I informed my people, and they said: We have believed you, but we shall meet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, we met him. Ghifar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Dharr has told us what you told him, and we have accepted Islam and testify that you are the Messenger of Allah. Then Aslam of Khuza'ah came forward and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have desired and entered into what our brothers and allies entered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam - may Allah grant them safety - and Ghifar - may Allah forgive them. Then Abu Bakr took my hand and said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service, O Abu Bakr. He said: Did you used to devote yourself to worship in your pre-Islamic days? I said: Yes; you would have seen me standing at the sun, praying continuously until its heat hurt me, then falling as if a covering. He said to me: In which direction did you face? I said: I did not know except wherever Allah directed me, until Allah brought Islam to me. No one narrated it from Urwah ibn Ruwaym except Abu Tarfah Abbad ibn al-Rayyan, and no one narrated it from Abbad except al-Walid; Muhammad ibn Aidh is alone in narrating it."
"61","61 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father Abd Allah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, that he heard al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrating, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: O son of Adam, if you give surplus it is better for you, and if you withhold it it is worse for you; begin with those you support; and Allah does not blame for sufficiency; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. No one narrated it from al-Qasim except Abd Allah ibn al-Ala."
"62","62 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzab narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is that it will be said: Did I not keep your body healthy? And quench you with cold water? No one narrated it from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzab except Abd Allah ibn al-Ala."
"63","63 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father Abd Allah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from al-Zuhri and al-Awza'i, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Ansari narrated to me. He said: My father narrated to me, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign he undertook, and the people were struck by hunger, so the people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for permission to slaughter some of their riding animals. The Messenger of Allah was about to permit them, when Umar ibn al-Khattab said: What do you think, O Messenger of Allah, if we slaughter our mounts, then meet our enemy tomorrow while we are hungry on foot? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you suggest, O Umar? He said: Call the people with the remnants of their provisions, then supplicate for blessing in them for us, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will surely suffice us through your supplication, if Allah wills. He said: It was as if a covering had been upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was lifted. So he called for a cloth and ordered it spread, then called the people with the remnants of their provisions, and they brought what they had; some brought a handful of food or a bowl, and some brought the like of an egg. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it placed upon that cloth, then supplicated for blessing in it and spoke what Allah willed him to speak, then called out to the army and they came, then he ordered them and they ate, were fed, and filled their vessels and bags. Then he called for a small water-skin and it was placed before him, then he called for water and poured it in, then rinsed his mouth in it and spoke what Allah willed him to speak, then inserted his little finger in it. I swear by Allah, I saw the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gushing springs of water. Then he ordered the people, and they drank, gave drink, and filled their skins and water-vessels. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared. He said: I testify that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; no one meets Allah with them on the Day of Resurrection except that he enters Paradise, whatever he may have done. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd Allah ibn al-Ala; his son is alone in narrating it from him."
"64","64 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Ya'la ibn Ata al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abu Khalaf, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of slaves, animals, or children has bad character, recite in his ears: Do you seek other than the religion of Allah? This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"65","65 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Ya'la ibn Ata al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar Abbad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Taymi narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the milk of a foolish woman for nursing. No one narrated it from Salim ibn Abd Allah except Abu Ma'mar, and no one narrated it from Abu Ma'mar except al-Hakam ibn Ya'la; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in narrating it."
"66","66 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi al-Muta, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us one morning and gave us an admonition that made hearts tremble and eyes shed tears, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you have admonished us with the admonition of one bidding farewell, so entrust us with a covenant. He said: Upon you is the fear of Allah, and listening and obeying, even if an Abyssinian slave; and those of you who remain after me will see severe disagreement, so upon you is my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided rightly-guiding caliphs, and bite upon it with the molars; and beware of newly-invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi al-Muta except Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr."
"67","67 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Ubayd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what is lawful for me and what is unlawful for me. So he looked me up and down and said: A small sprout. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a sprout of good or a sprout of evil? He said: Rather a sprout of good; do not eat the flesh of the domestic donkey, nor any beast with fangs. Abd Allah ibn al-Ala said: And Busr ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah, the like of it. No one narrated it from Muslim ibn Mishkam except Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr."
"68","68 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Busr ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Hassan ibn al-Damri, from Abd Allah ibn al-Sa'di, he said: We came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah, seven or eight, each seeking a need, and I was the last of them to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah, I left those behind me, and they claim that migration has ceased. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your need is better than their needs; migration will not cease as long as the disbelievers are fought. No one narrated it from Hassan except Abu Idris."
"69","69 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you points his spear at a man, and its blade is at the hollow of his throat, and he says: There is no god but Allah, let him lift the spear from him."
"70","70 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that Iyad ibn Himar al-Nahshali presented a horse as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I dislike the froth of the polytheists. No one narrated these two hadiths from Sufyan except al-Salt ibn Abd al-Rahman; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in narrating them."
"71","71 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands level with his shoulders when he said takbir, when he bowed, and when he prostrated. No one narrated it from Ibn Ajlan except Maslamah."
"72","72 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu al-Darda, he said: I asked Aishah about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: His character was the Quran; he became angry at its anger and pleased at its pleasure. It is not narrated from Abu al-Darda, from Aishah, except with this chain; Zayd ibn Waqid is alone in narrating it."
"73","73 - Ahmad ibn Ismail ibn Mahdi al-Sakuni narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-San'ani narrated to us, from Ma'mar and Ibn Shawdhab and Hammad ibn Salamah, all of them, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he takes them off, let him begin with the left."
"74","74 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Sa'id al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih and Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is entrusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."
"75","75 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Sa'id al-Qadi, at Hims, narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined his fingers together between his knees in bowing. No one narrated it from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Hammad ibn Salamah, and no one narrated it from Hammad except Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj."
"76","76 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Sa'id al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Ziyad al-Tasti narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two; when you fear the morning, pray witr with one. No one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abbad ibn Abbad; al-Fadl ibn Ziyad is alone in narrating it."
"77","77 - Ahmad ibn Ziyad al-Hadhdha al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad al-A'war narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sits in a gathering in which his idle talk is much, let him say before he stands: Glory be to You and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You; for he will be forgiven for what occurred in that gathering."
"78","78 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Jumahi al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from one hole twice. No one narrated it from Kathir except al-Hunayni."
"79","79 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the night and day is two by two. No one narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Umar except al-Hunayni."
"80","80 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the pilgrim in ihram does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers, and whoever does not find sandals, let him wear socks. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah and Abu Shihab al-Hannat."
"81","81 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih al-Hasan ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn Salman narrated to us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, he said: I heard Abu Musa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and a caller will call: Is it not justice from Me that I entrust every people with what they used to worship? Then their gods will be raised for them, and they will follow them, until none remains except the believers. It will be said to them: What is the matter with you? They will say: We do not see our God whom we used to worship. He said: Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them. No one narrated this hadith from Furat ibn Salman except Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi."
"82","82 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Su'ayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn al-Ahnaf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Which land is most sacred? It was said: Makkah. He said: Which month is most sacred? He said: Dhu al-Hijjah. He said: Which day is most sacred? He said: The Day of Sacrifice, the Day of the Greater Hajj. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. So I do not consider it right that blood be shed in the sanctuary of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Furat ibn al-Ahnaf except Malik ibn Su'ayr; Abu Ubaydah is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain."
"83","83 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Bakr ibn Bakkar al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, he said: Mujashi ibn Amr al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, that a son of his died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to him consoling him for his son, writing to him: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, to Mu'adh ibn Jabal, peace be upon you, for I praise to you Allah besides whom there is no god; to proceed: May Allah magnify your reward for you, inspire you with patience, and grant us and you gratitude; for our souls, wealth, families, and children are among the pleasant gifts of Allah and His entrusted loans. He gave you enjoyment through him in happiness and joy, and took him from you for great reward: prayer, mercy, and guidance. If you seek reward for him, be patient, and let not your impatience nullify your reward so that you regret; know that impatience does not bring back the dead nor repel grief, and whatever is to come, it is as if it has already come. Peace be upon you. This hadith is not narrated from Mu'adh except with this chain; Mujashi is alone in narrating it."
"84","84 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor of the Muslims enter Paradise five hundred years before their rich. We said: And who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: They are those who, when there is destruction, are sent into it, and when there is booty, others besides them are sent; those who are kept back at doors. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Abu Sa'id."
"85","85 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wakes in the morning and forgets, then eats or drinks while fasting, it is Allah who fed him and gave him drink. No one narrated it from al-Layth ibn Sa'd except his son Shu'ayb."
"86","86 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Waqqar narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Yazid, from Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Hashim, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, O Safiyyah, aunt of the Messenger of Allah, O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, let me not know you coming tomorrow carrying this world while people come carrying the Hereafter; my allies among you on the Day of Resurrection are only the God-fearing; my example among you is like a man giving sincere counsel to his people: he came to them and said: O people, you have been attacked, you have been overwhelmed; O morning calamity, I am the warner, death is the raider, and the Hour is the appointed time. No one narrated it from Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad except Nafi ibn Yazid, and no one narrated it from Nafi except Uthman ibn Kulayb; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Waqqar is alone in narrating it."
"87","87 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit occasionally and love will increase. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Yazid ibn Abi Habib, and no one narrated it from Yazid except Ibn Lahi'ah; Rawh ibn Salah is alone in narrating it."
"88","88 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A time will come upon you in which nothing will be dearer than three: a lawful dirham, a brother whose company is enjoyed, or a Sunnah acted upon. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Rawh ibn Salah."
"89","89 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Tawus, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce for one who does not own, and no emancipation for one who does not own."
"90","90 - And he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: A man among us freed a slave while he had no wealth besides him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned him to slavery, then sold him."
"91","91 - And he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"92","92 - And he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah daughter of Umayyah ibn Khalaf, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not harm the living by the dead."
"93","93 - And he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. No one narrated these hadiths from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub except Rawh ibn Salah."
"94","94 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sun rises from the west, Iblis will fall prostrate, calling: My God, command me to prostrate to whomever You will. His cohorts will gather to him and say: O their master, what is this humility? He will say: I only asked my Lord to grant me respite until the appointed time, and this is the appointed time. Then the Beast of the Earth will emerge from a cleft in al-Safa; the first step it places will be at Antioch, then it will come to Iblis and strike him. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain; Uthman ibn Sa'id is alone in narrating it."
"95","95 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated on a muddy day, until I could see the trace of that on his forehead and nose. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Suwayd; Zuhayr ibn Abbad is alone in narrating it."
"96","96 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Nasih narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no man who teaches his child the Quran in this world except that his father will be crowned on the Day of Resurrection with a crown in Paradise, by which the people of Paradise will recognize him for teaching his child the Quran in this world. No one narrated it from Abbad ibn Abi Salih except Jabir ibn Sulaym; Musa is alone in narrating it."
"97","97 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met, they shook hands, and when they returned from a journey, they embraced. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb; Yahya al-Ju'fi is alone in narrating it."
"98","98 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ashras narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ashras."
"99","99 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Dahiri Abd Allah ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Walid ibn Uqbah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people of Paradise will look upon some people of the Fire and say: How did you enter the Fire? By Allah, we entered Paradise only through what we learned from you. They will say: We used to say and not do. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Abu Bakr al-Dahiri; Zuhayr is alone in narrating it."
"100","100 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father died and did not perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: What do you think, if your father had a debt and you settled it, would it be settled for him? He said: Yes. He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father. No one narrated it from Thabit except Abbad; Abu Sa'id is alone in narrating it."
"101","101 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Muadhdhin narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Remorse is repentance."
"102","102 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among sins are sins which neither prayer, fasting, Hajj, nor Umrah expiate. They said: Then what expiates them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Worries in seeking livelihood. No one narrated it from Malik except Yahya ibn Bukayr; Muhammad ibn Sallam is alone in narrating it. Ahmad ibn Yahya said: I said: How did you hear this from Ibn Bukayr when no one besides you heard it? He said: I was sitting with Ibn Bukayr when a man came and mentioned his poor condition, so Ibn Bukayr said: Malik narrated to us, and mentioned this hadith."
"103","103 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from Fatimah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever wears a ring of carnelian will continue to see good. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Abu Bakr ibn Shu'ayb; Zuhayr ibn Abbad is alone in narrating it."
"104","104 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yasin ibn Abi Zurarah narrated to us, he said: Fudalah ibn al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Basri, that Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to him, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd Allah ibn Ukaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: I had permitted you the skins of dead animals, so do not benefit from a dead animal by skin or sinew. No one narrated it from Abu Sa'id al-Basri except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Fudalah ibn al-Mufaddal is alone in narrating it, from his father."
"105","105 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Musa Abu Ya'qub al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Khalid ibn Sa'd, from Ghalib ibn Abjar, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In the black seed is healing from every disease except death. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr, from Aishah, except with this chain; Ubayd Allah ibn Musa is alone in narrating it."
"106","106 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral bier. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Mudar except Muhammad ibn Sufyan."
"107","107 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abbad al-Abbadani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from Yahya ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Qatadah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the Hour. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have you prepared for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those you love. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; Abu Sakhr is alone in narrating it."
"108","108 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: al-Yasa ibn Qays narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from al-Yasa except Abd al-Malik."
"109","109 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Bayan al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran Sa'id ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he complained of illness, would take a handful of black seed and drink water and honey over it. This hadith is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"110","110 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Abd Allah al-Junda'i, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No prize-contest is lawful except on a camel's foot, a hoof, or an arrow. No one narrated it from Abu Abd Allah al-Junda'i except Sulayman ibn Yasar, and no one narrated it from Ibn Yasar except Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman; al-Layth is alone in narrating it, from Ubayd Allah."
"111","111 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Abu al-Aswad, from Bukayr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man says to another: O disbeliever, disbelief has become incumbent upon one of them. No one narrated it from Bukayr except Abu al-Aswad, and no one narrated it from Abu al-Aswad except Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far; al-Layth is alone in narrating it."
"112","112 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Fudayl. He said: I heard Mu'awiyah - and with him was a lock of women's hair - say: The daughter of Qarazah informed me that women wear this, and out of Allah's mercy upon you I knew that because of what I have of knowledge about it; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever adds to his hair something that is not from it, he adds falsehood to it. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far; al-Layth is alone in narrating it."
"113","113 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The flank is the vein of the kidney; when it moves it harms its owner, so treat it with heated water. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahman; Muslim is alone in narrating it."
"114","114 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Amr ibn Uthman narrated to me, he said: My uncle Abu Muslim, guide of al-A'mash, narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril: Does your Lord pray? He said: Yes. I said: And what is His prayer? He said: Glorified, Holy; My mercy preceded My anger."
"115","115 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two prayers: prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and after dawn until the sun rises; and fasting on the day of Fitr and the day of Adha; and he said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt; and wearing one garment wrapped around the body; and that a man sit with his knees drawn up in a garment with nothing of it over his private part; and that a woman travel a distance of two days except with a husband or a mahram; and that a man set out on a journey except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"116","116 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ismail al-Sadafi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah forbade wine and its price, forbade swine and its price, and forbade dead meat and its price. No one narrated it from Abu al-Zinad except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, and no one narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab except Mu'awiyah ibn Salih; Ibn Wahb is alone in narrating it."
"117","117 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ismail al-Sadafi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, Abd Allah ibn Awn, and Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been exhausted. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Abu Talhah, who called out: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is impure. No one narrated it from Ibn Awn except Jarir; Ibn Wahb is alone in narrating it."
"118","118 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Umar Abu Salamah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Makhul, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal narrated to me that he attended the marriage of a man from the Ansar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon, married the Ansari, and said: Upon affection, goodness, and auspicious fortune; beat the drum over your companion. So they beat the drum over him, and baskets came with fruit and sugar, and it was scattered over them, but the people held back and did not snatch. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How beautiful is forbearance; will you not snatch? They said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbade us from plundering on such-and-such day. He said: I only forbade you the plundering of armies, and did not forbid you the snatching at wedding feasts; so snatch. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urging us on to that snatching, and we urging him on. No one narrated it from al-Awza'i except Bishr ibn Ibrahim."
"119","119 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to consider exception valid even after a year, then recited: And do not say of anything: I shall do that tomorrow, except if Allah wills; and remember your Lord when you forget - saying: When you remember. It was said to al-A'mash: Did you hear this from Mujahid? He said: al-Layth narrated it to me, from Mujahid. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Mu'awiyah; Yahya is alone in narrating it."
"120","120 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Arabi ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah al-Sabai, he said: Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, that his father Abd Allah ibn Umar said one day: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques. I said: As for me, I shall prevent my family; whoever wishes, let him prevent his family. My father turned to me and said: May Allah curse you, may Allah curse you, may Allah curse you; you hear me say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they not be prevented, yet you say: I shall surely prevent my family. Then he wept and stood up angry. No one narrated this hadith from Arabi ibn Mu'awiyah except Yahya ibn Bukayr."
"121","121 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath mentioned, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The muezzin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs except Yahya al-Ju'fi."
"122","122 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: Allah takes souls at death: he said: The souls of the living and the dead meet in sleep, and they question one another; then Allah keeps the souls of the dead and sends the souls of the living to their bodies. No one narrated it from Mutarrif except Musa."
"123","123 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are upon Bariq, a river at the gate of Paradise, in a green dome; their provision comes out to them from Paradise morning and evening. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq is alone in narrating it."
"124","124 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man pursued another man for a debt he was owed, pressing him insistently. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever demands, let him demand with decency, whether paid in full or not."
"125","125 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far narrated to me, he said: Damrah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and I had a small brother. He said: O Abu Umayr, what did the little sparrow do? No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Shawdhab except Damrah."
"126","126 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No retaliation is taken for a wound until it heals. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Anbasah ibn Sa'id, judge of Rayy, and no one narrated it from Anbasah except Ibn al-Mubarak; Mahdi ibn Ja'far is alone in narrating it."
"127","127 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the heads of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, sons of Ali ibn Abi Talib, shaved on their seventh day, then gave charity of its weight in silver, but did not find a sacrificial animal."
"128","128 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from al-Sharid, a man from al-Sadif, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"129","129 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used often to supplicate with these words: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety and grief, miserliness and cowardice, incapacity and laziness, the burden of debt, and the domination of men."
"130","130 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of al-Huraqah, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted says: I am the most self-sufficient of partners from association; whoever associates with Me, it is all his - whoever associates with Me, it is all his."
"131","131 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Rifa'ah ibn Rafi ibn Malik al-Zuraqi, he said: I heard my father say: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How are the people of Badr regarded among you? He said: They are our most excellent. Jibril said: And those angels who witnessed Badr are our most excellent."
"132","132 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Yuhannas, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When my Ummah walks with a swaggering gait, and Persia and Rome serve them, some of them will be set against others."
"133","133 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Umarah, from his father, from Uwaymir ibn Ashqar, that he slaughtered his sacrificial animal, made a dish from it, then brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What is this? He said: From my sacrifice. He said: When did you slaughter it? He said: Before I prayed. So he ordered him to repeat it."
"134","134 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Mazini, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he ordered the people to raise their hands in seeking rain, he was wearing a black cloak; he wanted to take its lower part to turn it over, but it was heavy for him and overcame him, so he took its edge from over his shoulders and switched the two sides, one upon the other, placing what had been toward the back outward. No one narrated these hadiths from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"135","135 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani and Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment or an army, he said: Fight in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not steal from booty, do not betray, do not mutilate, do not kill a child nor an old man. He would say to their commander: When you besiege a fortress or the people of a town, call them to one of three: to enter Islam, to pay the jizyah, or that you fight them. And when you besiege the people of a fortress or town, and they wish to come down upon the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, for you do not know whether you will hit the judgment of Allah concerning them or not; rather bring them down upon your judgment and the judgment of your companions. And when you besiege the people of a fortress or town, and they ask you to give them the protection of Allah and His Messenger, do not give them the protection of Allah and His Messenger, but give them your protection and the protection of your companions; for your breaking your protections and those of your fathers is better for you than breaking the protection of Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal except Khalid ibn Yazid; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"136","136 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek the hour hoped for on Friday, between the Asr prayer and the setting of the sun, and it is the measure of this - meaning: his fist. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Wardan except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"137","137 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayk narrated to me, from his father, that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman, and I was among those who stoned them. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"138","138 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, he said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping dates and raisins together, and grapes and fresh dates together. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"139","139 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Sa'id al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast all of Sha'ban except a little of it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala except Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah."
"140","140 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Sa'id al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, he said: I heard Abu Qatadah al-Ansari say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leading people in prayer with Umamah daughter of Abu al-As upon his shoulder; when he prostrated he put her down."
"141","141 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father died and did not perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: If your father had a debt, would you settle it? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Ubayd Allah ibn Amr."
"142","142 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We were one day with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Jews came in to him, and he saw them with white beards. He said: Why do you not dye? It was said: They dislike it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But you dye, and beware of black. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'd ibn Ishaq except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"143","143 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, raising it. He said: If the weeping of Dawud, peace be upon him, and the weeping of all the people of the earth together, were weighed against the weeping of Adam, it would not equal it. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Ahmad ibn Bashir; Yahya ibn Sulayman is alone in narrating it."
"144","144 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Tha'labi narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Sayf al-Dabbi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Hudhayfah, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, when shall we abandon enjoining good and forbidding evil, when they are the chief deeds of the righteous? He said: When there befalls you what befell Banu Israil. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and what befell Banu Israil? He said: When your best ones flatter your wicked ones, understanding becomes among your worst, and rule becomes among your youngest; then a trial will envelop you: you attack and are attacked. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Ammar ibn Sayf, and no one narrated it from Ammar except Abu Sa'id al-Tha'labi; Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi is alone in narrating it."
"145","145 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, that he heard Sallam ibn Salm mentioning, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, I have not been sent to any prophet dearer to me than you; shall I not teach you names from the names of Allah, among the most beloved of His names to Him to be called by? Say: O Light of the heavens and the earth, O Adornment of the heavens and the earth, O Compeller of the heavens and the earth, O Support of the heavens and the earth, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of majesty and honor, O Succor of those who cry for succor, O Helper of those who seek help, and Goal of the worshippers, Reliever of the distressed, Comforter of the grieved, Answerer of the supplication of the compelled, Remover of distress, O God of the worlds, O Most Merciful of the merciful. Every need is removed through You. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Sallam ibn Salm; al-Muharibi is alone in narrating it."
"146","146 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: Khalid ibn al-Walid complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about sleeplessness at night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you go to your bed, say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, and Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter, be for me a protector from the evil of Your creation. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah except al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr."
"147","147 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid and Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man on earth who supplicates to Allah with a supplication except that Allah gives it to him, or averts from him an equivalent amount of evil, so long as he does not supplicate for sin or for severing kinship, so long as he does not hasten. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is his hastening? He said: He says: I supplicated and supplicated, but it was not answered for me. Then a man from the people said: Then we shall supplicate abundantly, O Messenger of Allah, so he said: Allah gives more abundantly."
"148","148 - And from Zayd ibn Waqid and Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the soul of the believer is taken, the people of mercy from the servants of Allah meet it, just as you meet the bearer of glad tidings from the people of this world, and they say: Give your companion time to rest, for he is in severe distress. Then they ask him: What did so-and-so do, and so-and-so woman, did she marry? And when they ask him about a man who had died before him, he says: Alas, that one died before me. So they say: Indeed to Allah we belong and indeed to Him we return; he was taken to his mother al-Hawiyah (the Abyss); what an evil mother and what an evil caretaker. And he said: Your deeds are presented to your relatives and kinsfolk from the people of the Hereafter; if it is good, they rejoice and are gladdened, and they say: O Allah, this is Your bounty and Your mercy, so complete Your blessing upon him and cause him to die upon it. And the deed of the evildoer is presented to them, so they say: O Allah, inspire him to a righteous deed with which You are pleased and which brings him near to You. No one narrated these two hadiths from Makhul except Zayd ibn Waqid and Hisham ibn al-Ghaz; Maslamah ibn Ali alone narrated them."
"149","149 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: The most beloved of My servants to Me are those who hasten most to break the fast. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zubaydi except Maslamah ibn Ali."
"150","150 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi Sahl al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Part of the perfection of prayer is praying in sandals. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Ali ibn Asim; Musa ibn Abi Sahl alone narrated it."
"151","151 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi Sahl al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Bukayr al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah, and the people grieved over that, and her maternal uncle Uthman ibn Mazun and her brother Qudamah came to her; while they were with her, grieving, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Hafsah and said: O Hafsah, Jibril came to me just now and said: Allah conveys greetings of peace to you, and says to you: Take Hafsah back, for she fasts much and prays at night, and she is your wife in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; Musa ibn Abi Sahl alone narrated it."
"152","152 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are three whose sufferer is not to be visited for consolation: the one with inflamed eyes, the one with toothache, and the one with a boil. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Maslamah ibn Ali."
"153","153 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, he said: My brother Abu Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {The eye for the eye and the nose for the nose}. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abu Ali ibn Yazid, nor from Abu Ali except Yunus; Ibn al-Mubarak alone narrated it."
"154","154 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) detained a man on suspicion, then intercession was made for him, so he released him. No one narrated this hadith from Bahz except Mamar."
"155","155 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Najih narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Mishrah ibn Haan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah blesses with a favor, and he wishes for it to remain, let him say abundantly: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {And why, when you entered your garden, did you not say: What Allah wills; there is no power except through Allah}. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Lahiah except Khalid ibn Najih."
"156","156 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ibn Ulayyah; Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan alone narrated it."
"157","157 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Zura Amr ibn Jabir, from Umar ibn Ali, from his father Ali ibn Abi Talib, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is the Mahdi from us or from others, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Rather from us; through us Allah will seal as through us He began, and through us they are rescued from polytheism, and through us Allah will reconcile their hearts after clear enmity, just as through us He reconciled their hearts after the enmity of polytheism. Ali said: Believers or disbelievers? So he said: Tempted, and a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Zura Amr ibn Jabir except Ibn Lahiah; Muhammad ibn Sufyan alone narrated it."
"158","158 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abdullah ibn Salam, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about the first of the signs of the Hour, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of the signs of the Hour is a fire that will emerge from the east and gather them toward the west. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar."
"159","159 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from a man - and he is Umar ibn Harun al-Balkhi - from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays on the night of al-Fitr and al-Adha, his heart will not die on the day hearts die. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Umar ibn Harun; Jarir alone narrated it."
"160","160 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abdus ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Abu Qabil, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The slogan of my nation when they are carried over the Bridge (al-Sirat) is: O there is no god but You."
"161","161 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah loves whoever loves dates. This hadith from Abdullah ibn Amr is not narrated except with this chain; Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan alone narrated it."
"162","162 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih al-Assal al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir al-Shabi, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar: How was the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Thirteen: eight, and he prays Witr with three, and two rakahs after dawn. Musa ibn Uqbah rendered it well, narrating it connected from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas. And Sharik narrated it from Abu Ishaq but did not connect it."
"163","163 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir al-Shabi, he said: I came to Madinah and asked about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they agreed upon thirteen, including the Witr, and two rakahs before dawn."
"164","164 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Salm narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Abu al-Anbas, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I used to scrape semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thus Misar narrated it from Abu al-Anbas, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Misar except Hafs ibn Salm; and Abu Nuaym narrated it from Abu al-Anbas but differed from Misar in its chain."
"165","165 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated it to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Anbas Said ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Aishah said: I used to scrape semen, and she gestured with her finger thus in her palm, meaning from the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"166","166 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar, so he made brotherhood between Sad ibn al-Rabi and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. Sad said to him: I have wealth, so it is half between me and you, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them is more beloved to you, and I shall divorce her, and when she becomes lawful, marry her. He said: May Allah bless for you your family and your wealth; show me the market. He did not return until he returned with dates and dried yogurt he had gained. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw on me a trace of yellow perfume, so he said: What is this? I said: I married a woman from the Ansar. He said: What did you give her as dowry? I said: The weight of a date-stone in gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"167","167 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: I ate a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there was no bread nor meat. I said: What was it, O Abu Hamzah? He said: Dates and sawiq (barley meal). No one narrated these two hadiths from Yahya ibn Said except Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"168","168 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ibn Shihab, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"169","169 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Said ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding ablution from what fire has touched. Al-Zuhri said: And Abu Sufyan is the son of the sister of Umm Habibah. No one narrated these two hadiths from Bakr ibn Sawadah except Jafar ibn Rabiah."
"170","170 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah and Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in a state of major impurity, then fast. No one narrated this hadith from Irak ibn Malik except Jafar ibn Rabiah."
"171","171 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in a state of major impurity from his wives, then begin that day fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah except Abu al-Zubayr, nor from Abu al-Zubayr except Khalid ibn Yazid; Bakr ibn Mudar alone narrated it."
"172","172 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Salih ibn Ata ibn Khabbab, freedman of Ibn Abi Diyab, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am the leader of the Messengers and no boast, and I am the seal of the Prophets and no boast, and I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted and no boast. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Salih ibn Ata, nor from Salih except Jafar ibn Rabiah; Bakr ibn Mudar alone narrated it."
"173","173 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Ziyad, from Nuh ibn Dhakwan, he said: And Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Prayer in the congregational mosque equals an obligatory prayer as an accepted Hajj, and a voluntary prayer as an accepted Hajj, and prayer in the congregational mosque is favored over other mosques by five hundred prayers. No one narrates this hadith from Nafi except Ata, nor from Ata except Nuh ibn Dhakwan; Zuhayr ibn Abbad alone narrated it."
"174","174 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Abu Qatadah, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinating facing the Qiblah. It is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"175","175 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge from seven deaths: from sudden death, from the bite of a snake, from being eaten by a beast, from drowning, from burning, from falling upon something or something falling upon him, and from being killed while fleeing from battle."
"176","176 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, he said: And Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to me, that he heard Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would not love to have the world and all it contains in exchange for this verse: {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah} - the verse."
"177","177 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Abd Rabbih ibn Said narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Shaqiq al-Azdi, from Ali ibn Rabiah, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib seated me behind him on a mule; when he placed his foot in the stirrup he said: In the name of Allah; when he sat upright he said: Praise be to Allah; when he was settled he said: Praise be to Allah who has subjected this for us, and we were not able to do it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return. Then he praised Allah three times, then magnified Allah three times, then said: O Allah, forgive me my sin, for none forgives sins except You. Then he laughed. I said to him: Why do you laugh? He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did the same, then laughed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you laugh? He said: I laughed at Allah's wonder at the servant who says: O Allah, forgive me my sin, for none forgives sins except You; Allah says: He knew that none forgives sins other than Me. No one narrated this hadith from Shaqiq al-Azdi - and he is Shaqiq ibn Abi Abdullah - except Yunus ibn Khabbab, nor from Yunus except Abd Rabbih ibn Said; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"178","178 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Abu al-Munayb, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you comes to his wife, let him cover himself, for if he does not cover himself, the angels are shy and depart, and Satan attends; and if there is a child between them, Satan is a partner in him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Abu al-Munayb al-Jurashi, nor from Abu al-Munayb except Ubaydullah ibn Zahr; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"179","179 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: When I take away the two beloved ones of My servant, and he is patient and seeks reward, I reward him for them with Paradise."
"180","180 - And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress of the Day of Resurrection; whoever covers the fault of a Muslim, Allah will cover his fault on the Day of Resurrection; whoever eases for a Muslim, Allah will ease for him on the Day of Resurrection; and Allah is in the aid of the servant so long as the servant is in the aid of his brother. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Said ibn Abi Maryam alone narrated them."
"181","181 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The likeness of Bilal is like a bee that goes out eating from the sweet and the bitter, then it is all sweet. This hadith from Abu Hurayrah is not narrated except with this chain; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"182","182 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, that while he was reciting Surah al-Baqarah with his horse tied, the horse moved about on its tether, so he raised his head, and behold a lamp-like object suspended between heaven and earth. So he went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so the Messenger of Allah said: Recite, O Usayd ibn Hudayr; do you know what it is? He said: No. He said: That is tranquility (al-sakinah); it drew near for your voice, and had you recited, the people would have woken looking at it. This hadith from Abu Said, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, is not narrated except with this chain; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"183","183 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub al-Makhzumi, he said: Abu Alqamah, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were praying after dawn, and said: There is no prayer after dawn except two rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub except Ubaydullah ibn Zahr; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"184","184 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sad, that Usamah ibn Zayd informed his father Sad, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I practice withdrawal (azl) from my wife. He said: Why? He said: Out of compassion for the child. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it were for that, then no; it would not have harmed Persia and Rome. This hadith from Usamah is not narrated except with this chain; Abu al-Nadr alone narrated it."
"185","185 - Ahmad ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dayli narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah was asked about withdrawal (azl), so he said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was not held against us. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr ibn Zayd except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"186","186 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer better than the dawn prayer on Friday in congregation, and I do not think any of you attends it except that he is forgiven. This hadith from Abu Ubaydah is not narrated except with this chain; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"187","187 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Abu Ushshanah narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever performs ablution well, then gathers his clothes upon him, then goes out to the mosque, ten good deeds are written for him for every step, and he remains in prayer so long as he waits for prayer, and he is recorded among those praying from the time he leaves his house until he returns. This hadith from Uqbah ibn Amir is not narrated except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Harith alone narrated it."
"188","188 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Say: He is Allah, One} equals a third of the Quran, and {Say: O disbelievers} equals a quarter of the Quran, and he used to recite them in the two rakahs of dawn, and he said: These two rakahs contain the desire of the age. No one narrated the first part of this hadith about {Say: He is Allah, One} and {Say: O disbelievers} from Layth except Ubaydullah ibn Zahr; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"189","189 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a qin (a small basket of dates) from every garden wall for the mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except al-Darawardi."
"190","190 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Said ibn Musa ibn Wardan, from his father Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah and Jabir ibn Abdullah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ali ibn Abi Talib is the keeper of my Pond on the Day of Resurrection, in it are cups like the number of stars, and the expanse of my Pond is between al-Jabiyah and Sanaa. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Wardan except his son Said, nor from Said except Ibn Lahiah; Rawh ibn Salah alone narrated it."
"191","191 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When Fatimah bint Asad ibn Hashim, mother of Ali, died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her and sat at her head, and said: May Allah have mercy on you, O my mother; you were my mother after my mother; you went hungry and fed me, you went unclothed and clothed me, you denied yourself good food and fed me, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the Abode of the Hereafter. Then he ordered that she be washed three times and three times, and when it reached the water containing camphor, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured it upon her with his hand, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took off his shirt and clothed her in it, and she was shrouded above it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Usamah ibn Zayd, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Umar ibn al-Khattab, and a black boy to dig, so they dug her grave; when they reached the niche, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug it with his hand and removed its soil with his hand. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered it and lay down in it, and said: Allah who gives life and causes death, and He is the Living who does not die, forgive my mother Fatimah bint Asad, and prompt her with her proof, and widen her entrance, by the right of Your Prophet and the Prophets before me, for You are the Most Merciful of the merciful. Then he magnified Allah over her four times, then they placed her in the grave, he and al-Abbas and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq - may Allah be pleased with them. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Sufyan al-Thawri; Rawh ibn Salah alone narrated it."
"192","192 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, he said: al-Qaqa ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about lost sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. And he was asked about lost camels? He said: What have you to do with it? It has its water-skin and its sandals; leave it until its owner comes to it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"193","193 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Rashid al-Barra narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qirdusi narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of these vegetables, let him not approach our mosque: garlic, leeks, onions, and radish, for the angels are harmed by what the children of Adam are harmed by. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Yahya ibn Rashid; Said ibn Ufayr alone narrated it."
"194","194 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hizami informed us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A great fat man will come on the Day of Resurrection weighing not even the wing of a gnat. Then he said: Recite: {And We shall assign no weight to them on the Day of Resurrection}. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman; Said ibn Abi Maryam alone narrated it."
"195","195 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Munayb al-Madani narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Abdullah ibn Atiyyah ibn Abdullah ibn Unays, he said: Abu Umamah ibn Thalabah informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes others than his patrons as patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah accepts from him neither compensation nor ransom. And whoever innovates an innovation in this city of mine or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither compensation nor ransom is accepted from him. This hadith from Abu Umamah ibn Thalabah is not narrated except with this chain; Abdullah ibn al-Munayb alone narrated it."
"196","196 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when the caller calls to prayer: O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, send blessings upon Muhammad and be pleased with me with a pleasure after which there is no anger, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will answer him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibn Lahiah, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"197","197 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Khunays ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Dajjal is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is: disbeliever, which the literate and the illiterate among the believers will read; with him are a garden and a fire, so his fire is a garden and his garden is a fire. This hadith from Muadh is not narrated except with this chain; Yahya ibn Bukayr alone narrated it."
"198","198 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah and Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from his father, he said: We used to consider showing off in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to be the major polytheism. No one narrated this hadith from Yala ibn Shaddad except Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah; Ibn Lahiah and Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"199","199 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Nadr say: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: Aishah said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, though he was with me on my bed, and I found him prostrating, facing the Qiblah with the tips of his toes, and I heard him say: I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, and in You from You; I praise You, I cannot encompass all that is in You. When he finished, he said: O Aishah, did your devil seize you? I said: Do you have a devil? He said: There is no son of Adam except that he has a devil. I said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And I, but I supplicated to Allah, so He aided me against him, so he submitted. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr Salim except Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"200","200 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Qurayt narrated to me, that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him, that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The five prayers are expiation for what is between them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Consider if a man had a workplace, and between his house and his workplace were five rivers; when he goes to his workplace he does what Allah wills, and dirt or sweat befalls him, and each time he passes a river he bathes - what would remain of his filth? Likewise the prayers: each time he commits a sin or what Allah wills, then prays and supplicates and seeks forgiveness, he is forgiven for what was in it. This hadith from Abu Said is not narrated except with this chain; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"201","201 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Rashid al-Muqri al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a Muhajir to sell for a Bedouin. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Abi Arubah; Sadaqah ibn Abdullah alone narrated it."
"202","202 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, the judge, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Rashid al-Muqri al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has conceived."
"203","203 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to change the religion of Ibrahim was Amr ibn Luhayy ibn Qamaah ibn Khindif, father of Khuzah. No one narrated this hadith from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, except Ibn Abi Dhib, nor from Ibn Abi Dhib except Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri; Hisham ibn Ammar alone narrated it."
"204","204 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin ibn Sad al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hammad ibn Abi Hazim al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Friday prayer is not obligatory upon five: the woman, the traveler, the slave, the child, and the people of the desert. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ibrahim ibn Hammad ibn Abi Hazim."
"205","205 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hammad ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has three sanctities; whoever preserves them, Allah preserves for him his religion and worldly affairs, and whoever neglects them, Allah preserves nothing for him. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The sanctity of Islam, my sanctity, and the sanctity of my kinship. No one narrated this hadith from Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab except Ibrahim ibn Hammad, and we know no other supported hadith of Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab besides this."
"206","206 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I read to Abdullah ibn Nafi, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no contagion, no Hama (owl omen), no Safar (month omen), and a sick camel is not to be brought to a healthy one. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ibn Nafi; Ahmad ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"207","207 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Berber's faith does not pass his collarbones. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhib except Abd al-Munim."
"208","208 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from his father, he said: al-Mustawrid al-Fihri said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say - and he mentioned Quraysh - and he said: Among them are four traits: they are the most upright of people at times of tribulation, the quickest of them to recover after calamity, the swiftest of them to attack after retreat, the best of them to the poor and orphan, and the strongest of them against the injustice of kings. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth except Ibn Wahb; Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth alone narrated it."
"209","209 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: My father Shuayb narrated to me, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi, from the people of Damascus, narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai and Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: Do not precede the month by a day or two, except a man who was fasting a fast, then let him fast it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth except his son Shuayb."
"210","210 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: al-Layth informed me, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari said: Ibn Jurayj claimed that Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to him, that a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I vowed to sacrifice myself. Ibn Abbas said: {Indeed in the Messenger of Allah you have a good example}, then he recited: {And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice} - with a ram, so he sacrificed it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except al-Layth, nor from al-Layth except Ibn Wahb; Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb alone narrated it."
"211","211 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, from Kab ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is as if you sprinkle them with arrows in what you say to them of poetry - meaning the satire of the polytheists. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Muhammad ibn Abdullah; Yaqub al-Zuhri alone narrated it."
"212","212 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Rishdin, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Umarah ibn Abdullah ibn Tumah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sacrificial animals among his companions, and gave me a young goat, and I found it to be a jadh (one year old), so I returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a jadh. He said: Sacrifice it."
"213","213 - And from Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that Sad ibn Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a vow that was upon his mother, so he said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"214","214 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya, scribe of al-Umari, narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: I found a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah, and he mentioned the hadith."
"215","215 - And from Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi, he said: A man peeked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind his curtain, while in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a comb, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known he was looking at me, I would have poked out his eye."
"216","216 - And from Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah, from his father and his uncle, that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and a man bit another man, who pulled his hand from his mouth, pulling out his front tooth. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking retaliation, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would he leave his hand in your mouth for you to crunch it as a stallion crunches? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled it."
"217","217 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughing so that I see his uvula; he would only smile, and when he saw clouds or wind, that was recognized on his face. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"218","218 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Udhrah ibn Musab ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: My father Musab ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Ata ibn Khalifah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, one drowned in the path of Allah is a martyr, and one who dies of stomach illness in the path of Allah is a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Khalifah except Abu al-Nadr."
"219","219 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Silver for silver, like for like, with no increase in it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Yazid ibn Abi Habib; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"220","220 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Saib, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abdullah, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, he said: My father taught me words, claiming that Umar ibn al-Khattab taught them to him, and Umar claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught them to him: Greetings, prayers, good and blessed things are for Allah; peace upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, and peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. This hadith from Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Umar, is not narrated except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"221","221 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Hayyan ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Mijlaz Lahiq ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black and his flag was white, with written upon it: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. This hadith from Ibn Abbas is not narrated except with this chain; Hayyan ibn Ubaydullah alone narrated it."
"222","222 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sells merchandise, let him not conceal a defect if there is one in it. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except Ibn Lahiah, and it is not narrated from Uqbah except with this chain."
"223","223 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I can almost see the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated. No one narrated this hadith from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, except Said ibn Abi Ayyub; Rawh ibn Salah alone narrated it."
"224","224 - And he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, from Umayr, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn al-Harith ibn al-Simmah, from his father, he said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had come out from relieving himself, and I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting until he placed his hand on a wall and wiped his face and his hands, then greeted me. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar except Said ibn Abi Ayyub; Rawh ibn Salah alone narrated it."
"225","225 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, freedman of Salamah, narrated to me, he said: Salamah ibn al-Akwa informed me, that on the day they conquered Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw fires blazing, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are these fires? They said: For the meat of domestic donkeys. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour out what is in them, and break them - meaning the pots. A man from the people said: Or shall we wash them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or that."
"226","226 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Ismail al-Sadafi narrated to us, he said: Dimam ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Wahib ibn Abdullah al-Maafiri, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate in {When the sky is rent asunder} and in {Read in the name of your Lord}. No one narrated this hadith from Wahib ibn Abdullah except Dimam; Yahya ibn Yazid al-Sadafi alone narrated it."
"227","227 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muti narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies without allegiance upon him dies the death of ignorance. No one narrated this hadith from Umayyah ibn Muhammad except Attaf ibn Khalid; Yahya ibn Bukayr alone narrated it."
"228","228 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Nasibi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is killed in blind turmoil by stoning among them, with a stone or a stick or a whip, it is accidental, its blood-money is that of accident. And whoever is killed deliberately, it is retaliation; whoever stands between him and it, upon him is the curse of Allah and His anger; neither compensation nor ransom is accepted from him. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hamzah al-Nasibi. And others narrated it from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas."
"229","229 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayrah, do not enter upon a ruler; and if you are overcome in that, do not go beyond my Sunnah, and do not fear his sword - and his sword is that you command them to fear Allah and obey Him. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abd al-Rahman; Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir alone narrated it."
"230","230 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad al-Muqad informed him, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, that he brought food near to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to his companions: Mention the name of Allah, and let each man eat from what is before him. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"231","231 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul while he was in shade, and he said: The son of Abu Kabshah has dusted upon us. His son Abdullah ibn Abdullah said: By Him who honored you and sent down the Book to you, if you wish, I shall bring you his head. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but be dutiful to your father and keep good company with him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Shabib ibn Said; Zayd ibn Bishr alone narrated it."
"232","232 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, that he heard Nafi narrating from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever inheritance was divided in ignorance (Jahiliyyah), it remains upon its division, and whatever inheritance Islam reached, it is upon the division of Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Uqayl, nor from Uqayl except Ibn Lahiah; Muhammad ibn Rumh alone narrated it."
"233","233 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Envy is only in two: a man to whom Allah gave the Quran, so he stands by it, permitting its lawful and forbidding its unlawful, and a man to whom Allah gave wealth, so he joins his relatives and kin with it and acts in obedience to Allah in it."
"234","234 - And from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who the Muslim is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: One from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe. They said: Who is the believer? He said: One whom people trust with their lives and wealth. They said: Who is the emigrant? He said: One who abandons evil and avoids it. No one narrated these two hadiths from Musa ibn Ulayy except Rawh ibn Salah."
"235","235 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, he said: Zuhrah ibn Mabad al-Qurashi narrated to me, that he used to go out with his grandfather Abdullah ibn Hisham to the market to buy food, and Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr would meet him and say: Include us, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has supplicated blessing for you. This hadith from Abdullah ibn Umar and Ibn al-Zubayr is not narrated except with this chain; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"236","236 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Amiri narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a woman from Khatham asked him for a ruling in the Farewell Hajj, saying: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has reached my father as a very old man unable to sit upright on a mount; will it suffice for him if I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Yes."
"237","237 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: May Allah reward Muhammad on our behalf as he deserves, tires seventy scribes for a thousand mornings. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Jafar ibn Muhammad, nor from Jafar except Muawiyah ibn Salih; Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil alone narrated it."
"238","238 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: I heard Misar ibn Kidam and al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, each narrating from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever falls ill or travels has the like of the reward he used to earn while healthy and resident. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Hafs ibn Ghiyath; Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hawari alone narrated it."
"239","239 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Misar, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hand, and he visited his wives, then began the morning in ihram."
"240","240 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bukayr al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves, so visit them, but do not speak foully; and I forbade you the meat of sacrifices, so eat and store; and I forbade you to make nabidh in vessels, so drink in whatever seems to you, but do not drink intoxicants. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Abdullah ibn Bukayr."
"241","241 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that her husband divorced her thrice, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"242","242 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Rabiah ibn Musa ibn Suwayd al-Jumahi narrated to me, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aflah, that a group of Companions sent me to Ibn Umar asking him about the middle prayer. He said: We used to say it is the prayer in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was directed to the Qiblah: al-Zuhr. This hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aflah, from Ibn Umar, is not narrated except with this chain; Musa ibn Rabiah alone narrated it."
"243","243 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu Mawdud Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sulayman al-Madani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Send blessings upon me abundantly on the radiant night and the bright day, for your blessings are presented to me."
"244","244 - And from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you stands for prayer, let him begin by leveling the place of his prostration, and not leave it until when he bends to prostrate he blows, then prostrates; let one of you prostrate upon a hot coal - it is better than prostrating upon his blowing."
"245","245 - And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is the best matter laid down, so whoever can increase, let him increase. These hadiths from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah, are not narrated except with this chain; Abu Mawdud alone narrated them."
"246","246 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Abi Rafi narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a ram, then said: This is on behalf of me and my nation. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"247","247 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Rabiah ibn Musa ibn Suwayd al-Jumahi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Yaqub al-Huraqi, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a believer meets a believer and greets him and takes his hand and shakes it, their sins fall away as the leaves of a tree fall. No one narrated this hadith from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid except Musa ibn Rabiah."
"248","248 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sallam al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abdullah al-Sakuni narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from his father, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a cloudy day on a journey facing other than the Qiblah; when he finished the prayer and greeted, the sun cleared, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed facing other than the Qiblah. He said: Your prayer has been raised in its truth to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except Ismail ibn Abdullah, nor from Ismail except Abu Dawud; Hisham ibn Sallam alone narrated it."
"249","249 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: al-Mualla ibn al-Walid al-Qaqaai narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, from his uncle Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from his father, and Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has placed truth upon the tongue and heart of Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman; al-Mualla ibn al-Walid alone narrated it."
"250","250 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, he said: Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you meets his brother in the day repeatedly, let him greet him."
"251","251 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that his term be extended and his provision widened, let him join his kinship. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Rishdin alone narrated it."
"252","252 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: When I afflict My servant with his two beloved ones (his eyes), then he is patient, I compensate him for them with Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muttalib except Ibn al-Had; Rishdin alone narrated it."
"253","253 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu Mawdud Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sulayman al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad al-Kharrat, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while Bilal was calling the iqamah for dawn, and he saw a man praying the two rakahs of dawn, so he said to him: Two prayers together? This hadith from Zayd ibn Thabit is not narrated except with this chain; Abd al-Munim ibn Bashir alone narrated it."
"254","254 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Umari, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Tufawi, he said: Ibn Umar would not mention the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that he wept. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Tafawi except Umar ibn Muhammad; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone narrated it."
"255","255 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, he said: Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Salih ibn Jabalah, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Mihran except Salih ibn Jabalah; Shihab ibn Khirash alone narrated it."
"256","256 - And from Salih ibn Jabalah, from Abu Qabil al-Misri, from Anas ibn Malik, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah builds for him a palace in Paradise of pearls, rubies, and peridot, and writes for him exemption from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Abu Qabil al-Maafiri, whose name is Hayy ibn Yuman."
"257","257 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: My uncle Abu Muslim, guide of al-Amash, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man from the people of al-Awali would invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at midnight for barley bread, and he would accept. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Muslim, nor from Abu Muslim except Amr ibn Uthman; Yahya ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"258","258 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who chants the talbiyah except that there chants with him, on his right and his left, stones and trees. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Salih except Ibn Wahb; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone narrated it."
"259","259 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind except Bakr ibn Sadaqah; Hamid ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"260","260 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Nasih narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn Burd except Musa ibn Nasih."
"261","261 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Malik ibn Anas mentioned, from Ismail ibn Abi Uways, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Uways except his son; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Malik ibn Anas alone narrated it."
"262","262 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not prefer some Prophets over others."
"263","263 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hunting its game between the two lava tracts of Madinah."
"264","264 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar used to pray before the sermon in the two Eids."
"265","265 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah above which there is no rank; so ask Allah to grant it to me."
"266","266 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Muawiyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Umra (a lifetime gift) is like inheritance."
"267","267 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr Salim, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Juhaym ibn al-Harith ibn al-Simmah al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For one passing in front of a praying person to wait forty is better for him than to pass in front of him."
"268","268 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Abu al-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The surplus water of a well is not to be withheld."
"269","269 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Speech is according to what you know."
"270","270 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Sahl, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm nor causing harm."
"271","271 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about divining with lines in sand? He said: It is a remnant of knowledge."
"272","272 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Kathir, freedman of Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed in the path of Allah, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled; there is neither gold nor silver there - meaning they are good and bad deeds."
"273","273 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Mihsan ibn Ali, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from his father, from Ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One who remembers Allah among the heedless is like one who is patient among those fleeing."
"274","274 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander of ten or more except that he comes bound on the Day of Resurrection; Allah pardons him as He wills, or punishes him as He wills."
"275","275 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Usayd ibn Abi Usayd al-Barrad al-Madani, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever abandons Friday prayer three times without excuse, Allah seals his heart."
"276","276 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed a horned, wide-eyed, uncastrated ram."
"277","277 - And from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A believer does not misappropriate spoils."
"278","278 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tooth-stick is purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord. No one narrated these hadiths from Said ibn Abi Ayyub except Rawh ibn Salah."
"279","279 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Hassan al-Kalbi, from Hudayj ibn Sawmi al-Himyari, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is hearing and obeying in what you love and hate, in your activity and reluctance, and in preference over you, and do not dispute the matter with its people. No one narrated this hadith from Sahl ibn Hassan al-Kalbi except Abu Shurayh."
"280","280 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the people of Hell are driven to it, it will meet them and scorch them with a scorch that leaves no flesh upon a bone except casting it upon the heel. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl except Abu Sinan; Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani alone narrated it."
"281","281 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, he said: al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from al-Awzai, from a man of the people of Madinah called Dawud ibn Ata, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give Zakat al-Fitr as a sa of dates or a sa of barley. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth ibn Sad except his son."
"282","282 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Thawban and Ibn Lahiah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyr feels not the pain of killing except as one of you feels the touch of a pinch. This hadith from Abu Qatadah is not narrated except with this chain; Isa ibn Hammad alone narrated it."
"283","283 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Humayd al-Mahri narrated to us, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever recites {Say: He is Allah, One} ten times, a palace is built for him in Paradise; whoever recites it twenty times, two palaces are built for him; and whoever recites it thirty times, three are built for him. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhrah ibn Mabad with connected chain except Khalid ibn Humayd; Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil alone narrated it."
"284","284 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muslim ibn al-Walid ibn Rabah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for a woman to fast while her husband is present except with his permission, nor to permit a man in her house while he dislikes it, and whatever she gives in charity from what she earns, he has half the reward of her charity."
"285","285 - And from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Woman was created from a crooked rib; you cannot keep her company except with crookedness in it; if you go to straighten her, you break her, and your breaking her is divorcing her. No one narrated these two hadiths from Muslim ibn al-Walid ibn Rabah except Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had."
"286","286 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Bashir al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not weep over religion when you entrust it to its people, but weep over it when you entrust it to others than its people. This hadith from Abu Ayyub is not narrated except with this chain; Hatim alone narrated it."
"287","287 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Zura Amr ibn Jabir, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will emerge from the east paving the way for the authority of the Mahdi. This hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Harith is not narrated except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"288","288 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Tarif ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, he said: There is no man who is entrusted with ten except that he is brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand bound to his neck, until judgment is passed between him and them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except al-Muharibi; al-Jufi alone narrated it."
"289","289 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: al-Layth, son of the daughter of al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, narrated to me, he said: Aishah bint Yunus, wife of Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, narrated to me, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me in my life."
"290","290 - And from al-Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The wide-eyed maidens of Paradise were created from saffron. These two hadiths from Layth are not narrated except with this chain; Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Ansari alone narrated them."
"291","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart. No one narrated this hadith from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman except Ibn Abi Hazim."
"292","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari narrated to us, saying: Abu Shakir Abdullah ibn Hassan ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from his father, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ruqaysh, that he heard his maternal uncle Abdullah ibn Abi Ahmad ibn Jahsh saying: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: I memorized six things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): there is no divorce except after marriage, no emancipation except after ownership, no fulfilling a vow in disobedience, no orphanhood after puberty, no (vowed) silence for a day until night, and no wisal (continuous fasting without break) in fasting. Ahmad ibn Salih said: Abdullah ibn Abi Ahmad ibn Jahsh is among the senior Tabiin of Madinah; he met Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he is older than Said ibn al-Musayyab. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Abi Ahmad except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"293","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Hubayrah and al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the end of time there will be a tribulation in which people are sifted as gold and silver are sifted in the mine. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"294","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever eats with his left hand, a devil eats with him, and whoever drinks with his left hand, a devil drinks with him. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim except Musa ibn Sarjis, and no one narrated it from Musa except Yazid ibn al-Had; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"295","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hammad ibn Abi Hazim al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Musab ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinating while standing."
"296","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection walking, barefoot, uncircumcised. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will women look at men? He said: For every man among them on that day will be a matter to occupy him. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Musab ibn Thabit except by Ibrahim ibn Hammad, and no one narrated them from Abu Hazim except Musab ibn Thabit."
"297","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, saying: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu Sakhr, from Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Hurmuz, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet would almost crack; then later he became heavy, and he would pray sitting, and when he wanted to conclude the surah he would stand and complete it, then bow. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Hurmuz except Rishdin; Zuhayr ibn Abbad alone narrated it."
"298","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Maqil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds during turmoil (al-harj) are like emigration to me. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Yahya ibn Uqbah."
"299","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No nation that was ever transformed (into animals) has offspring. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Zubaydi."
"300","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, saying: al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from al-Awzai, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Yaman al-Madini narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, that Humayd al-Tawil informed them that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man staggering between his two sons, and he asked about him. They said: He vowed to perform Hajj on foot. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no need for this man torturing himself, and he ordered him to ride. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth ibn Sad except his son."
"301","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah, who said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, saying: Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of abundant wealth have taken the reward; they pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and they have surplus wealth, while we have nothing to give in charity. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not teach you words by which you catch up with those who preceded you, and none who come after you will catch up with you except one who does the like of your deed? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Glorify Allah (say Allahu Akbar) thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him (say alhamdulillah) thirty-three times, declare His transcendence (say subhanallah) thirty-three times, and seal it with: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is capable of all things. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Rishdin."
"302","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and shook his hand; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not withdraw his hand from the man's hand until the man withdrew his hand. Then he said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Uthman has come. He said: A man of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Rawh ibn Salah."
"303","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, saying: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast with some people, he would say: The fasting ones have broken their fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have descended upon you. No one narrated this hadith from Waki, from Sufyan, except Zuhayr ibn Abbad. And people narrated it from Waki, from Hisham, without mentioning Sufyan."
"304","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Humran ibn Aban, from Uthman ibn Affan, that he performed ablution three times three times, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, his sins exit from his face, his hands, and his feet. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Sufyan; Hamid ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"305","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud narrated to us, saying: My grandmother Umm Abi, Umm Abdullah bint Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, narrated to me, saying: I heard my father Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah saying: I asked my father Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud: What do you remember of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I remember that he took me when I was five or six years old, seated me in his lap, wiped my head with his hand, and supplicated for blessing for me and for my offspring after me. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Utbah except with this chain; Musa ibn Awn alone narrated it."
"306","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Kalai narrated to us, saying: Zayn ibn Shuayb al-Iskandarani narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gharar sales (sales involving undue uncertainty)."
"307","And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pebble sales (al-hasah)."
"308","And from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The one who strives for the widow and the needy is like the warrior in the path of Allah."
"309","And from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathing on Friday is obligatory upon every mature person."
"310","And from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the Quran, when its keeper binds himself to it, standing with it by night and day, is like the parable of hobbled camels: if their keeper binds them he holds them, but if he releases their hobbles they go away; likewise is the keeper of the Quran."
"311","And from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: when he heard the hadith of Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting out land, Ibn Umar said: We used to rent it out for the rabi (produce) of the water-channel and for some of the straw that comes out of it."
"312","And from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade milking people's livestock except with their permission. No one narrated these hadiths from Usamah ibn Zayd except Zayn ibn Shuayb; Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Kalai alone narrated them."
"313","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Lakhmi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah - I think - from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he saw the crescent he would say: A crescent of good and right guidance; I believe in the One who created you and proportioned you. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Zuhayr."
"314","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed the tenth for rain-fed and river-irrigated produce, and half the tenth for what is irrigated by drawing water. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except Ibn Lahiah; Ibn Abi Maryam alone narrated it. He said:"
"315","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Amr al-Maafiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This nation will not abandon anything of the practices of the former peoples until it adopts them. This hadith is not narrated from al-Mustawrid except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"316","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Aziz Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reads a letter of the Quran, a good deed is written for him; and I do not say Alif Lam Mim Dhalika al-Kitab (as one), but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, Mim is a letter, Dhal is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Kaf is a letter. This hadith is not narrated from Awf ibn Malik except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Bilal alone narrated it."
"317","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, that he heard Zayd ibn Thabit saying: I used to write down the Quran - the hadith."
"318","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Jami ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah while around the House there were three hundred and sixty idols; he began striking them with a stick in his hand, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing, and: Truth has come, and falsehood neither originates nor restores. No one narrated this hadith from Jami ibn Abi Rashid except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Abu Salih al-Harrani alone narrated it."
"319","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Hisham, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was holding the hand of Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, you are more beloved to me than everything except myself. He said: No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, until I am more beloved to you than yourself. Umar said: Then you are now more beloved to me than myself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now, O Umar."
"320","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A neck will emerge from the Fire, having a tongue with which it speaks and two eyes with which it sees, and it will say: I have been commanded (to seize) every tyrannical obstinate one, whoever called upon another god with Allah, and whoever killed a soul without right."
"321","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is praying, let him not raise his sight to the sky; let it not be snatched away. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Said, except Yazid ibn Abi Habib; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"322","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, saying: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar, the freedman of Ghufr, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I never saw anyone whose prayer more resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this youth, meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. No one narrated this hadith from Rabiah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar; Rishdin alone narrated it."
"323","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Wahb, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night while I lay across between him and the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Rabiah except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"324","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Kalai narrated to us, saying: Zayn ibn Shuayb al-Iskandarani narrated to us, from Abu Ma'dan Amir ibn Murrah, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Hanzalah ibn Qays al-Zuraqi, from Rafi ibn Khadij, who said: We used to rent out our land, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that. Ahmad ibn Rishdin said: Abu Ma'dan was in Makkah, of great standing. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ma'dan except Zayn ibn Shuayb."
"325","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man keeps asking until he comes on the Day of Resurrection with not a shred of flesh on his face. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar."
"326","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Yusuf ibn Hashim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ashari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever visits a sick person, seventy thousand angels are assigned to him, praying for him. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ishaq ibn Abdullah; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"327","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him that Busr ibn Said narrated to him, from Mamar ibn Abdullah al-Adawi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Food for food, like for like. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"328","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Rishdin, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Abi Hakim, from Abu al-Nadr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever eats of this tree, let him not approach our mosque until its smell has left him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Jubayr ibn Hakim, and no one narrated it from Jubayr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Rishdin alone narrated it."
"329","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Yahya, the scribe of al-Umari, narrated to us, saying: Rishdin narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a saffron-dyed garment; he disliked it when he saw it on me, and said: These are only the garments of the disbelievers."
"330","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, saying: Muhammad ibn Aflah, the freedman of Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I bear witness to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I heard him saying: Indeed Allah does not love the obscene, foul-mouthed person. This hadith is not narrated from Usamah except with this chain."
"331","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr and Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thief is not cut except for the price of a shield and above: a quarter dinar and upward. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Ibn Lahiah."
"332","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih and Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The hand is not cut except for a quarter dinar and above. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Yasar except Bukayr, and no one narrated it from Bukayr except Makhramah."
"333","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Aishah, if obscenity were a man it would be an evil man, and if modesty were a man it would be a truthful man. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"334","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Aishah, who said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands before he poured forth (for the circumambulation). No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except Abdullah ibn Amir; Ibn Abi Hazim alone narrated it."
"335","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ayyub ibn Musa, that Yazid ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An aqiqah is offered for the boy, and his head is not touched with blood."
"336","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In camels there is a fara, and in sheep there is a fara. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Ayyub ibn Musa except by Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb alone narrated them."
"337","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: Ashhab ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us that Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to him, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Muhassir, he moved his mount and said: Upon you is the pebbles of khadhf (small pebbles). No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except Ibn Lahiah; Ashhab alone narrated it."
"338","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Khalid al-Rabai al-Marwazi narrated to me, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it not that one of you may take a flock of sheep at a distance of two or three miles, then Friday comes and he does not attend it three times, so Allah seals his heart."
"339","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Ali al-Bajali narrated to me, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two earrings of the Throne, and they are not suspended; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise settle in Paradise, Paradise will say: O Lord, You promised me that You would adorn me with two of Your pillars. He said: Did I not adorn you with al-Hasan and al-Husayn. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Ibn Lahiah except by Humayd ibn Ali."
"340","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by him while he was praying sitting, and said: The sitting one has half the prayer of the standing one. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Isa ibn Yunus; Abu Salih al-Harrani alone narrated it."
"341","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, who said: The Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the dowries of women is twelve uqiyyahs, and the uqiyyah is forty dirhams, so that is four hundred and eighty. And the Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding bathing from major impurity is a sa, and ablution two ratls; and the sa is eight ratls. And the Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding what the earth produces of wheat, barley, raisins, and dates, when it reaches five awsuq - and the wasq is sixty sa - so that is three hundred sa, with this sa by which the Sunnah was established. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir except Salih ibn Musa."
"342","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, saying: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None weeps except one of two men: an evildoer completing his evildoing, or a righteous man completing his righteousness."
"343","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Rishdin, saying: Abu Isa the muezzin Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Marzuq al-Tujibi, from Sahl ibn Alqamah al-Nasai, from Abu Uthman al-Tunbudhi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, Allah removes the light of faith from his belly."
"344","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Sulayman Qubbaytah narrated to us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Uqbah, from Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wore a turban would let its end hang in front and behind. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Salih except al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin, and it is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain."
"345","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, saying: Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Wardan narrated to me, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hand them over to them as long as they pray the five, meaning the charities to the rulers. This hadith is not narrated from Sad, raised to the Prophet, except with this chain; Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil alone narrated it."
"346","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abi al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman the nephew of Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, and she said: Where are you from? I said: From the people of Kufah. She said: Are you those who revile the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: We know of no one who reviles the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Rather - do you not curse Ali, and curse whoever loves him? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love him. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman the nephew of Zayd ibn Arqam except Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, and no one narrated it from Yazid except Amr ibn Abi al-Miqdam; Yusuf ibn Adi alone narrated it."
"347","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Fadalah ibn al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, saying: Maruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, from Abu Ushshanah, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever here is from Ma'add, let him stand. So I started to stand, and he said: Sit. Then he said it a second time, so I stood, and he said: Sit. Then he said it a third time, so I stood, and he said: Sit. I said: Who are we, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You are from Qudaah ibn Malik ibn Himyar. No one narrated this hadith from Maruf ibn Suwayd except Ibn Lahiah; Fadalah ibn al-Mufaddal alone narrated it, from his father."
"348","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Buraydah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Of whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. No one narrated this hadith from Tawus except his son, and no one narrated it from Ibn Tawus except Mamar and Ibn Uyaynah; Abd al-Razzaq alone narrated it."
"349","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: al-Bara ibn Abdullah al-Ghanawi narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating, from Ibn Abbas, that when Umar ibn al-Khattab was made caliph, he forbade people from mutah of women, and said: This was only something permitted to people when people were few; then it was forbidden to them after that, so I will not find anyone doing that today except I mete out punishment to him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Nadrah except al-Bara ibn Abdullah."
"350","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh narrated to me, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of Allah's servants in rank on the Day of Resurrection is a just, gentle ruler, and the worst of Allah's servants with Allah in rank on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust, harsh ruler. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"351","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Zayd, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lashed eighty for wine. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"352","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning in a state of major impurity from his wives, then complete his fast. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah except Abu al-Zubayr; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"353","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Rabiah informed me, from Irak ibn Malik and Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"354","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"355","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like."
"356","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with a qussah (a lock of added hair) and said: The women of the Children of Israil used to place this in their heads, so they were cursed, and the mosques were forbidden to them. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah, from Ibn Abbas, except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"357","And from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fitrah is five: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, the siwak, trimming the nails, and plucking the armpit. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"358","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: al-Rabi ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: al-Shafii narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer is better than the prayer of a lone individual by twenty-five degrees. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except al-Shafii."
"359","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abu Salih Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Wahwah al-Ansari, from his father, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Baqi al-Gharqad, performed ablution, washed his face and his hands, wiped his head, took water with his right hand and sprinkled it upon his feet, then washed them. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn except Ibn Lahiah."
"360","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that some Muslims were with the polytheists, swelling the numbers of the polytheists; an arrow comes, shot, striking one of them and killing him, or he is struck and killed, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning them: Those whom the angels take while wronging themselves, they say: wherein were you; they say: we were weak in the land - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aswad except Ibn Lahiah."
"361","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abu Salih Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is his leaving what does not concern him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, except Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar and Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"362","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani, from Aishah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, whoever is in charge of my nation and is gentle with my nation, be gentle with him, and whoever is harsh upon them, be harsh upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Ibn Lahiah. And the name of Abu Ali al-Hamdani is Thumamah ibn Shufi."
"363","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Dinar, from Abu Yazid al-Khawlani, from Fadalah ibn Ubayd, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The martyrs are three: a believing man of sound faith who meets the enemy and is truthful to Allah until he is killed - people will crane their necks toward him on the Day of Resurrection; a believing man of sound faith who meets the enemy and a stray arrow comes to him and kills him - he is in the second rank; and a believing man who was excessive against himself, meets the enemy and is truthful to Allah until he is killed - he is in the third rank. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"364","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ablution is required from what fire has touched. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah; Ibn al-Mubarak alone narrated it."
"365","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi informed us, saying: Dawud ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Umar ibn al-Khattab, and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned the gravest of the major sins, but they had no knowledge of them, so they sent me to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As to ask him about that. He informed me that the gravest of the major sins is drinking wine. I came to them and informed them, but they denied that and all leapt up to him. He informed them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A king from the Children of Israil seized a man and gave him a choice between drinking wine, killing a boy, committing fornication, eating pork, or they would kill him if he refused. He chose to drink wine, and when he drank, he did not refrain from anything they wanted from him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us then: No one drinks it and has his prayer accepted for forty nights, nor dies with any of it in his bladder except Paradise is forbidden to him; and if he dies within the forty, he dies the death of ignorance. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, except with this chain; al-Darawardi alone narrated it."
"366","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi informed us, saying: Dawud ibn Salih narrated to us, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the cat: It is not impure."
"367","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Abi Zaynab informed me, from Hasan ibn Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wherever you are, send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me. This hadith is not narrated from al-Hasan ibn Ali except with this chain; Ibn Abi Maryam alone narrated it."
"368","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Himyari al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abdullah al-Jafari narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from al-Hasan except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Amr al-Himyari alone narrated it."
"369","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, saying: al-Amash, Misar ibn Kidam, and Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque of Mina when some Bedouins came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to man? He said: Good character. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath ibn Sawwar except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"370","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer who mixes with people so they harm him, and he is patient over their harm, is better than the believer who does not mix with people so they harm him, and he is patient over their harm. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Habib, except Abu Bakr al-Dahiri; Zuhayr ibn Abbad alone narrated it."
"371","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Dinar, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a choice, so we chose him, and that was not counted as a divorce. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Jubayr except Ata ibn Dinar; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"372","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Firas and Bayan, from al-Shabi, from Wahb ibn Khanbash, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Firas, except Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban; Hamid ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"373","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, saying: Umm Abdullah the daughter of Khalid ibn Ma'dan narrated to me, from her father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see a red column toward the east in Ramadan, store up your year's food, for it is a year of hunger. No one narrated this hadith from Umm Abdullah the daughter of Khalid except Bishr ibn Bakr; Zayd ibn Bishr alone narrated it."
"374","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani, from al-Haytham ibn Shufi, from Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ten of his companions - Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, al-Zubayr, and others - were on Mount Hira, it shook beneath them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still, Hira, for there is none upon you but a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Sad except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"375","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Wahb, from Rabah ibn Ubaydah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man passes in front of one of you while he is praying, let him repel him; if he refuses, let him strive against him. No one narrated this hadith from Rabah ibn Ubaydah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said, except Amr ibn Uthman ibn Mawhab; al-Qasim ibn Malik alone narrated it."
"376","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Jabir al-Saidi narrated to us, from his father Isa ibn Jabir, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Shihab, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba and the muzaffat to be used for nabidh."
"377","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Shihab, that Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan narrated to him that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand, wheat for wheat is usury except hand to hand, and dates for dates is usury except hand to hand."
"378","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe in a qadah, which is the faraq, and I used to bathe with him from a single vessel."
"379","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send sacrificial animals from Madinah, and I would twist their garlands, then he would not avoid anything that the pilgrim in ihram avoids."
"380","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that Aishah said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated after she had performed the ifadah. I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is she detaining us? I said: O Messenger of Allah, she had already performed the ifadah, circumambulated the House, and menstruated after the ifadah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then let her depart."
"381","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Shihab, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a woman of Khatham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling during the Farewell Hajj - while al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has come upon my father as a very old man who cannot sit upright on a mount; will it suffice for him if I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"382","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Shihab, that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that Bashir ibn Sad came with al-Numan to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have gifted this slave of mine to my son. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you gifted all your children? He said: No. He said: Then take it back."
"383","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever pollinates a palm tree then sells its root, its fruit belongs to the one who pollinated, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"384","And with his chain, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he met Umar ibn al-Khattab in a riding party - while Umar was swearing by his father - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Verily Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers; whoever would swear, let him swear by Allah, otherwise let him be silent."
"385","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that some men among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were shown Laylat al-Qadr in a dream as being in the last seven of Ramadan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see your dreams have coincided regarding the last seven, so whoever seeks it, let him seek it in the last seven."
"386","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you should make a man rise from his seat and then sit in it."
"387","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you should outbid his brother, nor should one of you propose over the proposal of his brother."
"388","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The one who misses the Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth were destroyed."
"389","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), facing the east, saying: Verily tribulation is here, verily tribulation is here, from where the horn of Satan rises."
"390","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any jointly-owned slave among partners whose one owner frees his share, its value is assessed for the one who freed, and he frees fully if his wealth reaches it."
"391","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day; and he used to order us to follow dogs and kill them wherever we found them in Madinah."
"392","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, informing him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not right for a Muslim man who has something to bequeath to spend two nights except with his will written at his head."
"393","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Amir ibn Rabiah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees a funeral, if he is not walking with it, let him stand until it passes by or is set down before that."
"394","And with his chain, from Ayyub, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of one who gives charity then takes back his charity is like the dog that vomits then returns to its vomit. None narrated these hadiths from Ayyub ibn Musa except Isa ibn Jabir al-Saidi; his son alone narrated them from him, and none wrote them down except Ibn Rishdin."
"395","Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatadah and Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The righteous dream is from Allah, grief-inducing dreams are from Satan, and part of dreams is what a man tells himself. If one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him stand and pray two rakahs. And I dislike the yoke in sleep, and the shackle pleases me, for it is firmness in religion; and the believer's dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood; in the end of time the believer's dream will hardly lie, and the most truthful of you in dreams is the most truthful of you in speech. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar, from Qatadah, except Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Abdullah ibn Jafar alone narrated it."
"396","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Hammad, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when bowing or prostrating, used to say: Glory be to You and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, and no one narrated it from Zayd except Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Abdullah ibn Jafar alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Masud except with this chain."
"397","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Mujahid, saying: The son of Rafi ibn Khadij narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us something that was beneficial to us - and the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is upon the head and the eye: he forbade us to accept land for some of its produce or for coined silver, and forbade us the earnings of the cupper. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn, from Mujahid, from the son of Rafi, except Abu Awanah; Muhammad ibn Isa alone narrated it. And Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and others narrated it from Abu Husayn, from Mujahid, from Rafi himself."
"398","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Salim al-Aswad, from Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Hawd (fountain) is from Aden to Amman of al-Balqa; its water is sweeter than honey, more fragrant than musk, whiter than milk; its cups are as many as the stars of the sky; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst thereafter; the first people to come to it are the poor emigrants with disheveled heads and soiled clothes, who do not marry women of ease and for whom the gates are not opened. No one narrated this hadith from al-Abbas ibn Salim except Muhammad ibn Muhajir."
"399","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu Ubaydullah Muslim ibn Mishkam, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will surely find myself disputing over one of you at the Hawd, saying: This is of my companions, whereupon it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. Abu al-Darda said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah that He not make me of them. He said: You are not of them. No one narrated this hadith from Muslim ibn Mishkam except Yazid ibn Abi Maryam."
"400","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Awzai and Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you who act upon what they know and do what they are commanded; and after them will be rulers who act upon what they do not know and do what they are not commanded; whoever disapproves has been safe, but whoever is pleased and follows. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, except Maslamah. And al-Muafa ibn Imran and others narrated from al-Awzai, from Ibrahim ibn Murrah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah."
"401","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, saying: Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul on earth that dies having good with Allah that would love to return to you even if it had the world, except the martyr, for he loves to return and be killed another time, because of what he sees of the excellence of martyrdom. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Waqid except al-Haytham ibn Humayd."
"402","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his expeditions; we camped at a place and came to him there. He raised his hands and said: Faith and wisdom are here, toward Lakhm and Judham. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abu Kabshah, except Muhammad ibn Muhajir."
"403","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abidah, from Hayyan Abu al-Nadr, who said: I met Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am as My servant thinks of Me; if he thinks good, then good, and if he thinks evil, then evil. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abidah except Muhammad ibn Muhajir."
"404","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Amir ibn Zayd al-Bikali narrated to me that he heard Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami saying: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is your Hawd that you speak of? He said: Like between al-Bayda and Busra; Allah will extend for me in it a kira (riverbank) whose ends no created human knows where they are. Umar ibn al-Khattab exclaimed Allahu Akbar and said: As for the Hawd, the poor emigrants who fight in the path of Allah and die in the path of Allah will come to it; so I hope He grants me the kira to drink from it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord has promised me to admit to Paradise of my nation seventy thousand without reckoning, then every thousand will intercede for seventy thousand, then my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will scoop with His two hands three scoops. Umar exclaimed Allahu Akbar and said: The first seventy, Allah will cause them to intercede for their fathers, sons, and clans, and I hope Allah places me in one of the last scoops. The Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, is there fruit in it? He said: Yes, and in it is a tree called Tuba that corresponds to al-Firdaws. He said: Which tree of our land does it resemble? He said: It does not resemble any tree of your land, but have you been to al-Sham? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It resembles a tree in al-Sham called the walnut, growing on a single trunk, then its top spreads. He said: How great is its base? He said: If a young she-camel of your family's camels set out, it would not traverse it before its collarbone breaks from old age. He said: Is there grapes in it? He said: Yes. He said: How great is its cluster? He said: A month's journey for the pied crow, without turning or tiring. He said: How great is its berry? He said: Did your father ever slaughter something great of his sheep? He said: Yes. He said: Then he skinned its hide and gave it to your mother, saying: Tan this, then make for us from it a bucket with which we water our livestock? He said: Yes. He said: That would satisfy me and my household? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And your whole clan. This hadith is not narrated from Utbah ibn Abd except from the hadith of Zayd ibn Sallam, and none narrated it from Zayd except Muawiyah ibn Sallam and Yahya ibn Abi Kathir."
"405","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Abu Umamah al-Bahili narrated to me that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes. He said: How long between him and Nuh? He said: Ten centuries. He said: How long between Nuh and Ibrahim? He said: Ten centuries. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how many were the messengers? He said: Three hundred and fifteen. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Muawiyah ibn Sallam alone narrated it."
"406","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Abdullah ibn Ulayyah narrated to me that Qays al-Kindi narrated to him that Abu Said al-Anmari narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord has promised me to admit to Paradise of my nation seventy thousand without reckoning, and every thousand will intercede for seventy thousand, then my Lord will scoop three scoops with His two hands. Qays said: I said to Abu Said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, with my ears, and my heart retained it. Abu Said said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And that, Allah willing, encompasses the emigrants of my nation, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will complete the remainder from our Bedouins. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said al-Anmari except with this chain; Muawiyah ibn Sallam alone narrated it."
"407","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us that he heard Aishah narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every human of the children of Adam was created with three hundred and sixty joints."
"408","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: al-Hakam ibn Mina narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah narrated to him that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some people will surely stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or Allah will surely seal their hearts, then they will surely be of the heedless."
"409","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: al-Saluli narrated to me, from Sahl ibn al-Hanzaliyyah, that they traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn; they journeyed long until evening, and prayer came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A horseman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I went ahead of you until I climbed such-and-such mountain, and there were Hawazin upon their young camels, with their litters, cattle, and sheep, gathered at Hunayn. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: That is the spoils of the Muslims altogether, Allah willing. Then he said: Who will guard us tonight? Anas ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Ride. So he mounted his horse and came to the Messenger of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Face this ravine until you are at its top, and let us not be surprised from your direction tonight. In the morning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to his prayer place, prayed two rakahs, then said: Have you sensed your horseman? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not sensed him. The call for prayer was made, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while in prayer kept turning toward the ravine, until he finished his prayer and greeted, saying: Rejoice, your horseman has come to you. We looked through the trees in the ravine, and there he came until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I went until I was at the top of this ravine where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me; in the morning I climbed both paths, looked, and saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have made it obligatory (earned Paradise); it will not harm you to do no deed after it. This hadith is not narrated except with this chain; Muawiyah ibn Sallam alone narrated it."
"410","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Zakariyya al-Madaini narrated to us, saying: al-Zubayr ibn Said al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Salim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever licks honey three mornings every month, no great affliction will befall him."
"411","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah, its fodder and its traces are in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."
"412","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and a Bedouin met him, saying: When is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have prepared for it no good for which I praise myself, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love. Abu al-Malih narrated nothing from al-Zuhri, from Anas, other than this."
"413","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw on the night I was taken: men whose tongues were cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are preachers of your nation who command people what they do not do. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Isa ibn Yunus."
"414","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer's lower garment is to mid-calf, and there is no sin in what is between that and the ankles, and what is below the ankles is in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Nuaym al-Mujammir except al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman; Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah alone narrated it."
"415","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays Abu Zukayr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am not of frivolity, nor is frivolity of me. Meaning: I am not of falsehood, nor is falsehood of me. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Abi Amr except Abu Zukayr."
"416","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Muadh ibn Jabal to Yemen. I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise us. He said: Cooperate and do not differ, make easy and do not make difficult. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhayr except Amr ibn Uthman."
"417","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail, from his father, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bow, placing his hands upon his knees. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail, except Abu Awanah; Muhammad ibn Isa alone narrated it."
"418","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Qazaah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, saying: Suwayd ibn Hujayr narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed under a blind banner, fighting for a faction or supporting a faction, his death is that of ignorance. No one narrated this hadith from Suwayd ibn Hujayr except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Bahili; Qazaah ibn Suwayd alone narrated it."
"419","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Amrah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she had a sheep she used to milk; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed it and asked Umm Salamah about it. Umm Salamah said: It died, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Why did you not benefit from its skin? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its tanning makes it lawful, as vinegar of wine makes it lawful. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Faraj ibn Fadalah."
"420","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Matar ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anaq narrated to us, from Umm Aban bint al-Wazi ibn al-Zari, from her grandfather al-Zari - who was in the delegation of Abd al-Qays - who said: When we came to Madinah, we raced from our mounts to kiss the hands and feet of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while al-Mundhir al-Ashajj waited until he came to his baggage, put on his garment, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have two traits Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves: forbearance and deliberation. Al-Mundhir said: Praise be to Allah who fashioned me with two traits Allah and His Messenger love. No one narrated this hadith from Umm Aban except Matar ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"421","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and asked him about this verse: And fight them until there is no tribulation. Ibn Umar said: We fought with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until there was no tribulation; so go you and your companions and fight until there is tribulation. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Mihran except Abu al-Malih."
"422","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib dueled a man on the day of Mutah and killed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his ring and his spoils as extra. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Aqil except Sharik; Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Zurarah alone narrated it."
"423","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: al-Numan ibn Bashir narrated to me, saying: I was at the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man said: I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except giving drink to the pilgrims. Another said: I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except maintaining the Sacred Mosque. Another said: Striving in the path of Allah is better than what you said. Umar rebuked them, saying: Do not raise your voices at the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday; rather, when you have prayed Friday, I will enter and ask him about what you differed in. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Do you make the giving of drink to pilgrims and the maintaining of the Sacred Mosque like one who believes in Allah - the verse. This hadith is not narrated from al-Numan except with this chain."
"424","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, saying: al-Abbas ibn Salim narrated to me, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from Amr ibn Abasah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of his mission, when he was then in hiding. I said: What are you? He said: I am a prophet. I said: And what is a prophet? He said: The Messenger of Allah. I said: Did Allah send you? He said: Yes. I said: With what did He send you? He said: To worship Allah, break idols, and join kinship. I said: Well did He send you; who follows you in this? He said: A free man and a slave - meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. Amr ibn Abasah used to say: I am a fourth of Islam. So I embraced Islam, then said: Shall I follow you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but join your people; when you hear that we have prevailed, come to us. No one narrated this hadith from al-Abbas ibn Salim except Muhammad ibn Muhajir."
"425","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Rabiah, from Sa'dan ibn Salim, from Yazid ibn Abi Shaybah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the waist-wrapper applies to the shirt."
"426","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us, saying: Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Tammam ibn Najih, from Kab ibn Dhuhl, who said: I heard Abu al-Darda saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose from his seat intending to return to it, he would leave his sandals or some of what was upon him."
"427","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, saying: Bakkar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he directed a detachment in one of the directions; the bearer of glad tidings came to him bringing news that a woman had taken charge of the enemy's affair. He fell prostrate, then raised his head, saying: Men are ruined when they obey women."
"428","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, saying: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kulthum, from al-Awzai, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman with prolonged bleeding bathes from one menstrual period to the next. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Salamah ibn Kulthum; Baqiyyah alone narrated it."
"429","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: Rather I will supplicate Allah. Then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: Rather it is Allah who raises and lowers; I hope to meet Allah with no one having a claim of injustice against me. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from the hadith of al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"430","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Yunus al-Aftas narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that when he opened the prayer he would say: Glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise - like the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab; Yusuf ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"431","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Sari al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: Harun Abu al-Tayyib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begins with asking before greeting, do not answer him."
"432","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Sari al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Zakariyya al-Madaini narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Zadahn, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the last of this nation curses the first of it, whoever has knowledge let him manifest it, for the concealer of knowledge then is like the concealer of what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"433","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Shabib ibn Shaybah al-Sa'di narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakrah narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever kills a covenantee will not find the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found from a distance of five hundred years. No one narrated this hadith from Shabib ibn Shaybah except Muhammad ibn Said al-Qurashi."
"434","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating upon his forehead at the hairline. No one narrated this hadith from Hakim ibn Umayr except Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam."
"435","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about this verse: He is able to send upon you torment from above you or from beneath your feet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will happen, but its interpretation has not yet come. This hadith is not narrated from Sad except with this chain; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam alone narrated it."
"436","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be in the end of time a people who are brothers in public and enemies in secret."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and how will that be? He said: ""It will be due to the desire of some of them for others, and the fear of some of them from others."" This hadith is not narrated from Mu'adh except with this chain; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam is alone in transmitting it."
"437","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""I had intended to order the prayer to be established, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, then take bundles of firewood, then go to people in their houses who do not attend the prayer, and burn their houses over them."" No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"438","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, that a man from Thaqif known as Abu Tamam gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wineskin of wine as a gift, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has been made unlawful, O Abu Tamam."" He said to him: O Messenger of Allah, so may I spend its price? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Indeed the One who forbade drinking it forbade its price."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, and it is not narrated from Amir ibn Rabi'ah except with this chain."
"439","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: We would not keep the meat of the sacrifices beyond three days, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to eat and to take provision. No one narrated it from Zayd except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"440","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Malik al-Lakhmi, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks after the revelation of al-Ma'idah. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd ibn Malik except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"441","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Umayr, from al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b taught me the Qur'an, so I gave him a bow as a gift, and he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""You are wearing it from Hell."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, we sometimes attend their food and eat from it. He said: ""As for what was made for you, if you eat it you are only eating it in exchange for your reward, and as for what was made for others and you attended and ate from it, there is no harm in it."" This hadith is not narrated from al-Tufayl ibn Amr except with this chain; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"442","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Muhajir ibn Maymun, from Fatimah, that she said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Where is our mother Khadijah? He said: ""In a house of reed, in which there is no idle talk and no fatigue, between Maryam and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh."" She said: From this reed? He said: ""No, rather from reed strung with pearls, gems and sapphires."" This hadith is not narrated from Fatimah except with this chain; Safwan is alone in transmitting it."
"443","Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Mutarrif Abu Sufyan al-Saruji narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, he said: Abu Marwan al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade accepting the food of the corrupt. This hadith is not narrated from Imran ibn al-Husayn except with this chain; Abd al-Rahim ibn Mutarrif is alone in transmitting it."
"444","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, referring it to Abu Dharr, he said: When the last ten of Ramadan came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed i'tikaf in the mosque; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Asr prayer on the twenty-second day he said: ""We shall stand tonight, if Allah wills, so whoever wishes to stand, let him stand; it is the twenty-third night."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in congregation after the night prayer until a third of the night had gone, then he left. When the twenty-fourth night came he said nothing and did not stand. When the twenty-fifth night came, he stood after the Asr prayer of the twenty-fourth day and said: ""We shall stand tonight, if Allah wills"" - meaning the twenty-fifth night - ""so whoever wishes, let him stand."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed until half the night had gone. When the twenty-sixth night came he stood and said: ""We shall stand, if Allah wills"" - meaning the twenty-seventh night - ""so whoever wishes to stand, let him stand."" Abu Dharr said: So we exerted ourselves for standing, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us until two-thirds of the night had gone, then he withdrew to a dome in the mosque. I said to him: We had hoped, O Messenger of Allah, that you would lead us until morning. He said: ""O Abu Dharr, when you pray with your imam and leave when he leaves, the standing of your night is recorded for you."" No one narrated this hadith from Shurayh ibn Ubayd except Safwan ibn Amr."
"445","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd al-Kindi, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abu Rayhanah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever traces his lineage to nine unbelieving forefathers seeking honor through them, he is the tenth of them in the Fire."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rayhanah except with this chain; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"446","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Muhammad ibn Mu'adh ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu al-Mundhir, I have been commanded to present the Qur'an to you."" He said: In Allah I have believed, at your hands I submitted, and from you I learned. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated the statement. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and was I mentioned there? He said: ""Yes, by your name and lineage in the highest assembly."" He said: Then recite, O Messenger of Allah."
"447","And with his chain, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of fever? He said: ""Good deeds flow for its companion as long as a foot trembles over him, or a vein throbs over him."" So he said: O Allah, I ask You for a fever that does not prevent me from going out in Your path, nor going out to Your House, nor to the mosque of Your Prophet. So Ubayy was never touched except that fever was in him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Mu'adh ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayy except Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba'."
"448","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abu Wathimah al-Nasri, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When there comes to you one whose religion and character please you, then marry him; if you do not do so, there will be tribulation on earth and widespread corruption."" No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman."
"449","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nadabah narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in one of his expeditions: ""Take many of these sandals, for one of you remains mounted as long as they are on his feet."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Muthanna except al-Hasan ibn Habib."
"450","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Yunus al-Aftas, brother of Abu Muslim al-Mustamli, narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will call a servant from His servants, and he will be made to stand before Him, and He will ask him about his rank as He asks him about his wealth."" No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Yusuf ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"451","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah Abu Ya'qub al-Tamimi al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Hilal al-Wazzan, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""There is none among you but that his Lord, blessed and exalted, will ask him, saying: My servant, what deceived you concerning Me? What answer did you give to the messengers?"" No one narrated this hadith from Hilal al-Wazzan except Sharik; Ishaq ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"452","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Hisham al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the Isha prayer ""By the fig and the olive."" No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Ubayd ibn Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"453","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Tamimi al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is from the Sunnah not to go out on the day of Fitr until you eat, nor on the day of Sacrifice until you return. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ibn Ulayyah; Ishaq ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"454","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran his fingers through his beard. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Ismail ibn Ja'far; Ishaq ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"455","Ahmad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, he said: While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard the clamor of men behind him; when he finished his prayer he said: ""What is the matter with you?"" They said: We hurried to the prayer. He said: ""Do not do so; let each of you pray what he catches, and make up what he missed."" No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Shayban."
"456","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abdullah ibn Adi ibn al-Hamra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at al-Hazwarah and said: ""By Allah, I know that you are the best of Allah's land, and the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah; had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left."" No one narrated this hadith from the nephew of al-Zuhri except al-Darawardi."
"457","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim ibn Uwaym ibn Sa'idah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take virgins, for they are sweeter in mouths, more productive in wombs, and more content with little."""
"458","And from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted, chose me, and chose companions for me, and made among them for me ministers, supporters and in-laws; so whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people."" These two hadiths are not narrated from Uwaym ibn Sa'idah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi is alone in transmitting them."
"459","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Aslami narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted, is with the debtor until he pays his debt, so long as his debt is not in what Allah dislikes."" This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Ja'far except with this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in transmitting it."
"460","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Hammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they saw weakness in his standing and said: How feeble is so-and-so! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have eaten your brother and backbitten him."" No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Wardan except Hammad ibn Abi Humayd."
"461","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Rashid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is no divorce for one who does not own, and no emancipation for one who does not own."" No one narrated this hadith from Sadaqah ibn Yazid except Abdullah ibn Yazid."
"462","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah ibn Asim, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a black dark night; we stopped at a place, and a man would take stones, gather them as a prayer place and pray toward it. When morning came, we were facing other than the qiblah, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed this night of ours toward other than the qiblah. So Allah, exalted, revealed: ""And to Allah belong the east and the west, so wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah."" No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Ubaydullah except Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman."
"463","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Mahdi al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Awdi narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The first for whom depilatory paste was made and who entered the bathhouse was Sulayman ibn Dawud; when he entered it and felt its heat and distress, he said: Alas for the punishment of Allah, alas, alas, before 'alas' does not avail."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Mahdi is alone in transmitting it."
"464","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: Forty days was fixed for the woman in postpartum bleeding. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Abu Khalid."
"465","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Gentle dealing with people is charity."" No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Muhammad except Musa ibn Isa."
"466","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Azhar al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Salamah for household goods worth ten dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Amr ibn al-Azhar."
"467","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The sutrah of the imam is the sutrah of those behind him."" No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Suwayd; al-Rabi' is alone in transmitting it."
"468","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: Abdullah al-Hawzani narrated to me, that he met Bilal, the caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), using the toothstick in Aleppo. He said: I said: O Bilal, tell me how was the occupation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He had nothing; I was the one who managed that for him since Allah sent him until he died (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When a Muslim man came to him and he saw him naked, he would order me concerning him, so I would go, borrow, buy a cloak, clothe him and feed him, until a man from the polytheists met me and said to me: O Bilal, I have means, so do not borrow from anyone except from me; so I did. One day I performed ablution, then stood to call the prayer, and the polytheist came with a band of merchants. When he saw me he said: O Abyssinian. I said: At your service. He frowned at me and spoke harsh words, saying: Do you know how long between you and the month? I said: Near. He said: There are only four between you and it, then I will take you for what you owe me, for I did not give you what I gave out of your honor or the honor of your companion to me, but I gave you so that I may take you as a slave and send you back herding sheep for me as you used to herd before. Something entered my soul as enters the souls of people. So I went and called the prayer; when I had prayed the night prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his family. I asked permission to enter to him and he permitted me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheist from whom I used to borrow said to me such-and-such, and you have nothing to pay, nor do I, and he will disgrace me; so permit me to go to some of these tribes who have embraced Islam until Allah provides His Messenger with what he pays on his behalf. So I went out until I came to my house, placed my sword, bag and sandals at my head, and faced the horizon with my face. When I slept a while I woke, then night covered me and I slept until the first dawn broke. I wanted to go, when a man came hurrying, calling: O Bilal, answer the Messenger of Allah. So I went until I came to him, and there were four kneeling camels with their loads upon them. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked permission. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Rejoice, for Allah has brought you your payment."" So I praised Allah. He said: ""Did you not pass by the four kneeling camels?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""Their necks and what is upon them are yours; upon them are clothing and food given to me as a gift by the chief of Fadak, so take them, then pay your debt."" So I did: I unloaded their loads, fed them, then stood for the dawn call. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, I went out to al-Baqi', placed my fingers in my ears and called: Whoever claims a debt from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him attend. I kept selling and paying until no debt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained on earth, until two ounces or an ounce and a half remained in my hand. Then I went to the mosque when most of the day had gone, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque alone. I greeted him and he said to me: ""What happened to what was with you?"" I said: Allah has paid everything that was upon His Messenger; nothing remains. He said: ""Did anything remain?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""See that you relieve me of it, for I shall not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of it."" No one came to us until evening; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the night prayer he called me and said: ""What happened to what was with you?"" I said: It is with me; no one came to us. So he spent the night in the mosque until morning, and prayed the second day until at the end of the day two riders came; I took them, fed them and clothed them. When he prayed the night prayer he called me and said: ""What happened to what was with you?"" I said: Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah. So he said takbir and praised Allah out of fear that death would overtake him while that was with him. Then I followed him until he came to his wives, greeting each wife until he came to his lodging. This is what you asked me about (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Bilal except with this chain; Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam is alone in transmitting it."
"469","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: Abu Asma al-Rahbi narrated to me, that Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I was standing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a scholar from the Jewish scholars came and said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. So I pushed him a push that nearly made him fall, and I said to him: Why do you not say: O Messenger of Allah? The Jew said: We only call him by the name his family gave him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My name is Muhammad, which my family gave me."" The Jew said: I have come to ask you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Will it benefit you if I tell you?"" He said: I shall hear with my ears. So he tapped with a stick he had and said: ""Ask."" The Jew said: Where will the people be on the day the earth is changed to other than the earth, and the heavens? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They will be in darkness before the bridge."" He said: Who will be the first of people to cross? He said: ""The poor of the emigrants."" The Jew said: What will be their greeting when they enter Paradise? He said: ""The extra lobe of the fish's liver."" He said: What will be their meal after it? He said: ""The whale of Paradise which eats from its ends will be slaughtered for them."" He said: What will be their drink over it? He said: ""From a spring called Salsabil."" He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: And I have come to ask you about something which no one on earth knows except a prophet, or one man, or two men. He said: ""Will it benefit you if I tell you?"" He said: I shall hear with my ears. He said: I have come to ask you about the child. He said: ""The man's fluid is white and the woman's fluid is yellow; when they meet and the man's semen overcomes the woman's semen, they bear a male by Allah's permission, and when the woman's semen overcomes the man's semen, they bear a female by Allah's permission."" The Jew said: You have spoken the truth, and indeed you are a prophet. Then he left and went. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He asked me about what he asked me, and I had no knowledge of any of it until Allah brought it to me."" This hadith is not narrated in its entirety from Thawban except with this chain; Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam is alone in transmitting it."
"470","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Recite the Qur'an, for it will come on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for its companions. Recite the two radiant ones: Surah al-Baqarah and Surah Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two shades, or as if they were two flocks of birds in ranks, arguing on behalf of their companions. Recite Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing, leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it."" No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya."
"471","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When my community does fifteen traits, affliction will befall it."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are they? He said: ""When spoils are passed around, trusts are taken as booty, zakah is a burden, a man obeys his wife and disobeys his mother, voices are raised in the mosques, a man honors his friend and shuns his father, a man is honored out of fear of his evil, the leader of the people is the vilest of them, singing girls and musical instruments are taken, wines are drunk, and silk is worn - then expect transformation and swallowing."" No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Faraj ibn Fadalah."
"472","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr, how will you be when you are among the dregs of people?"" And he interlaced his fingers. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me? He said: ""Patience, patience; mix with people in their manners, but oppose them in their deeds."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain; Abu Tawbah is alone in transmitting it."
"473","And with it, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever wakes with his concern the world, he is in nothing from Allah; whoever does not care for the Muslims is not of them; and whoever willingly submits to humiliation without compulsion is not of us."" This hadith is not narrated except with this chain; Yazid ibn Rabi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"474","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Shu'aythi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Azhar, from Ibn Awn, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: ""Or a trace of knowledge"" - he said: ""Good handwriting."" No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Amr ibn al-Azhar."
"475","Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Busr: Where is our state compared to the state of those before us? He said: ""Glory be to Allah; by Allah, if they were raised from the graves they would not recognize you except that they find you standing praying."" No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Busr except Yazid ibn Khumayr; Safwan ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"476","Ahmad ibn Fil al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Any man who is given a life-grant, it is his and his descendants after him; it is inherited by whoever inherits from his descendants; and whoever is given a watching-grant, it is like the life-grant."" Thus Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated it, from Ibn al-Zubayr."
"477","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows, for part of the excellence of prayer is straightening the row."" No one narrated it from Mis'ar except Bishr ibn al-Sari, and no one narrated it from Bishr except Ibn Abi Umar."
"478","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When there are three, two should not converse privately excluding one."" No one narrated it from Ibn Ajlan except his son Abdullah."
"479","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Abidi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, you are more beloved to me than myself, and you are more beloved to me than my family, and more beloved to me than my child; when I am in the house and remember you, I cannot bear it until I come to you and look at you; and when I remember my death and your death, I know that when you enter Paradise you will be raised with the prophets, and if I enter Paradise I fear I shall not see you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him until Gabriel came down with this verse: ""And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, they will be with those upon whom Allah has bestowed favor, of the prophets and the truthful"" - the verse."
"480","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, the Prophet said: ""There is no prescribed punishment on the slave woman until she is married; when she is married with a husband, upon her is half of what is upon married women."""
"481","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth."
"482","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abu Alqamah al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever touches his private part, ablution has become obligatory upon him."" No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Abu Alqamah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"483","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Salimi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man will enter Paradise, and no household or chamber in Paradise will remain but they will say: Welcome, welcome, to us, to us."" Abu Bakr said: What do you think of this man on that day? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, and you are he, O Abu Bakr."""
"484","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, from his father, from his mother Umm Kulthum, she said: Busrah bint Safwan came to me and told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Who proposes to Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah?"" I said: So-and-so and so-and-so. He said: ""Where are you from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf? For he is the chief of the Muslims and the best of them."""
"485","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go around his wives in one washing. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'mar, from Thabit, except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Sufyan al-Thawri and others narrated it from Ma'mar, from Qatadah."
"486","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when his caller came to him with the night prayer on a night of wind and rain, would order him to follow his call with: ""Pray in your dwellings."""
"487","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from his uncle Abu Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you know what the likeness of this fire of yours is to the fire of Hell? It is blacker than the smoke of this fire of yours by seventy times."" No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ma'n; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"488","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, says: A servant whose body I have kept sound and whose provision I have widened, who does not come to Me in every four years, is deprived."" No one raised this hadith from Sufyan except Abd al-Razzaq."
"489","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are most beloved to you? He said: ""Aishah."" They said: We do not mean among women. He said: ""Then her father."""
"490","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take it, O sons of Talhah, abiding and inherited; none will take it from you except a wrongdoer"" - meaning the custody of the Ka'bah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal; Ma'n ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"491","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent three men to Caesar, to Khosrau, and to the ruler of Alexandria, and sent Amr ibn al-As to the Negus. When Amr came to the Negus he found those with him entering bowing through a low door; when Amr saw the low door and their entering to him, he turned his back, then entered walking backward. When he had entered through it he straightened; the Abyssinians were alarmed and intended to kill him. They said: What prevented you from entering as we entered? He said: We do not do that to our Prophet, and he is more deserving that it be done to him. The Negus said: Leave him; he has spoken the truth. This hadith is not narrated from Amr ibn Umayyah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"492","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he left the two Eids, come to the middle of the prayer place, stand, look at the people how they leave and what their demeanor is. Then he would wait a while, then leave. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"493","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Abi Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and we entered with him, through the gate of Banu Abd Manaf, which people call the gate of Banu Shaybah, and we left with him to Madinah through the gate of al-Hazwarah, which is the gate of the tailors. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Abdullah ibn Nafi'; Marwan ibn Abi Marwan is alone in transmitting it."
"494","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Abu al-Umays, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, that when he touched the Stone he would say: ""O Allah, with faith in You, belief in Your Book, and following the Sunnah of Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" We do not know that Abu al-Umays reported any hadith from Abu Ishaq except this; no one narrated it from Abu al-Umays except Hafs, and no one from Hafs except Ibrahim al-Shafi'i."
"495","Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn Harun al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Nafi', freedman of Ibn Umar, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best rows of men are the first of them, and the worst are the last of them; and the best rows of women are the last of them, and the worst are the first of them."" This hadith is not narrated from Umar ibn al-Khattab except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it. And with it."
"496","Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your span among the nations that passed is as between the Asr prayer and sunset."" No one narrated it from Malik except Ma'n; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"497","Ahmad ibn Muhammad Abu Sulayman al-Qazzaz al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If he refuses, repel him; if he refuses, fight him, for he is only a devil"" - meaning concerning one who passes in front of the praying person. No one narrated it from Safwan except al-Darawardi."
"498","Ahmad ibn Zakariyya al-Abidi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When supper is present and the prayer is established, begin with supper."" No one narrated this hadith from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"499","Ahmad ibn Zakariyya al-Abidi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Fulayh al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Muslim al-Khashshab narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O sons of Abd Manaf, O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, if you are given charge of this matter, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House from praying at any hour he wishes, by night or day."" No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, except Sulaym ibn Muslim."
"500","Ahmad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself."" No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, except al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar."
"501","Ahmad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Makkah; Allah made it sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by Allah's sanctity until the Day of Resurrection: its grass shall not be cut, its trees shall not be lopped, its game shall not be disturbed, and its lost property shall not be lawful except for one who announces it. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir. He said: Except idhkhir. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"502","Ahmad ibn Zakariyya al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him ahead from Muzdalifah to Mina among the weak of his family. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Bishr."
"503","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, brother of Abu Ma'mar, narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sent to me inviting me to suhur, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called it the blessed morning meal. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except from this angle; we know no one narrated it from Ibn Uyaynah except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, brother of Abu Ma'mar Isa ibn al-Sari al-Hajwani, a Kufan."
"504","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night, his toothstick and his ablution water were placed for him. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'd except Zurarah, nor from Zurarah except Bahz; Hammad ibn Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"505","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We used to pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-Mukhtar except Mansur; Sa'id ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it."
"506","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah narrated to us, he said: Artah Abu Hatim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No one has a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr; he supported me with his wealth and himself, and married his daughter to me."" No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Artah; Muhammad ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"507","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: Hashim, a companion of Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father Abu Layla, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on an expedition, and the pots boiled with the meat of domestic donkeys, so he ordered us to overturn them, and apportioned a sheep for every ten of us. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid except Hashim, this shaykh; Muhammad ibn Imran is alone in transmitting it."
"508","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The Muslim does not inherit the unbeliever, nor the unbeliever the Muslim."" No one narrated this hadith from Qays except Ali ibn al-Ja'd."
"509","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays al-Tahi narrated to us, he said: Thumamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Umm Sulaym sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), having made a watbah for him. I sought him and found him in the house of a slave of his, a tailor, who had made food for him containing hump and pumpkin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began eating the pumpkin and moving the hump aside with his forefinger. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym has made a watbah for you and would like you to eat from it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and ate from it. She said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Anas - supplicate to Allah for him. He said: ""O Allah, prolong his life, increase his wealth and children, and forgive him."""
"510","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mu'adh al-A'war, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would order killing them; so kill from them every jet-black one."" Amr said to him: Who narrated to you? He said: By Allah, Abdullah ibn Mughaffal narrated it to me. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'adh al-A'war except Hammad ibn Zayd; Khalid ibn Khidash is alone in transmitting it."
"511","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb dictated to me from memory, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no cutting on the plunderer, nor the embezzler, nor the traitor."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Ibn Wahb; Abu Ma'mar is alone in transmitting it."
"512","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Ghadidi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one in ihram shall not marry, nor propose, nor shall a proposal be made over him; none of you shall sell over his brother's sale, nor propose over his brother's proposal until he permits him."" No one narrated this hadith from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Umar; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it."
"513","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, brother of Juwayriyah, from Juwayriyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left nothing on the day he died except a white mule, his weapons, and land he made as charity. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Isra'il; Mu'ammal is alone in transmitting it."
"514","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: al-Bakhtari narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Ramadan is the cry, in Dhu al-Qa'dah the tribes are distinguished, and in Dhu al-Hijjah the pilgrim is robbed."" No one narrated this hadith from Shahr ibn Hawshab except al-Bakhtari; Nuh ibn Qays is alone in transmitting it."
"515","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When a woman leaves her house while her husband dislikes that, every angel in heaven curses her, and everything she passes, except jinn and men, until she returns."" No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Zayd; Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"516","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asari narrated to us, he said: Ghalib al-Qattan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he entered upon Aishah one morning, and she said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, teach me the name of Allah by which when He is called He answers, and when He is asked He gives. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his face away. So she stood, performed ablution, and said: O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and by Your Great Name by which when You are called You answer, and when You are asked You give. He said: ""By Allah, it is indeed among these names."" No one narrated this hadith from Ghalib al-Qattan except Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asari; al-Qawariri is alone in transmitting it."
"517","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I sat in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sitting I never sat before or after more pleasing to me: the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while people near his chamber were disputing about the Qur'an. He came out of the house as if pomegranate seeds had been crushed on his face, or as if blood were dripping from his face, and said: ""O people, were you commanded with this, to dispute the Qur'an, part of it with part? The Qur'an was not revealed for one part to belie another; if it is allegorical, then believe in it."" No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except his son; Amr al-Naqid is alone in transmitting it."
"518","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, that he heard Ubadah narrate, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Wheat for barley, two for one, hand to hand, and deferred is not lawful."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"519","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isa ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: He said, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women, in prayer."" No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Marwan; Isa ibn al-Musawir is alone in transmitting it."
"520","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Ismail, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Advise me. He said: ""Leave hearsay, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except al-Sari ibn Ismail."
"521","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When deficiency befell the Children of Israel, a man would see his brother in sin and forbid him, then meet him the next day and what he saw would not prevent him from being his companion, eating and drinking with him. So Allah struck the hearts of some of them upon others, and the Qur'an came down concerning them: 'Cursed were those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel upon the tongue of Dawud and Isa son of Maryam' - the verse - to His saying: 'Many of them are defiantly disobedient.' Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'No, by the One in whose Hand is my soul, until you seize the wrongdoer by his hands and bend him to the truth forcefully.'"" No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abd al-Kabir al-Hanafi, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, and al-Ashja'i."
"522","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, he said: Shuja' ibn al-Walid Abu Badr narrated to us, he said: al-Ruhayl ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution, would run his fingers through his beard. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ruhayl except Shuja' ibn al-Walid."
"523","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, all from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage except with the permission of a guiding guardian, or a ruler."" No one narrated this hadith ascribed from Sufyan except Ibn Dawud, Bishr and Ibn Mahdi; al-Qawariri is alone in transmitting it."
"524","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Baddi, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not trim his mustache is not of us."" No one narrated this hadith from Zakariyya ibn Yahya except Jarir."
"525","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, brother of Abu Ma'mar, narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says in the morning and evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing will harm him."""
"526","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isa ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - concerning Allah's saying, mighty and majestic: ""When the help of Allah comes, and the conquest"" - he said: ""The conquest of Mecca; the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was announced to him, so seek forgiveness from your Lord, and know that your term has come."" No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Suwayd."
"527","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Suwayd narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me during the Umrah of Hudaybiyah while the vermin of my head had multiplied, and said: ""O Ka'b, is this indeed a harm?"" I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, is there a concession? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons."" No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Suwayd."
"528","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle Isa ibn Musawir narrated to us, they said: Suwayd narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about found property found in inhabited land in a watercourse. He said: ""Announce it for a year; if its owner comes, otherwise it is yours."" And he was asked about found property found in enemy land, and said: ""Concerning it and buried treasure is the fifth."" And he was asked about the lost sheep, and said: ""Take it, for it is only yours, or your brother's, or the wolf's."" And he was asked about the lost camel, and said: ""Leave it, for it has its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees."" And he was asked about cattle stolen from the mountain pasture. He said: ""He is struck blows, and the fine is doubled upon him; if it is from the pen and reaches the price of a shield - which is a dinar - then cutting is due; if it is less than that, he is struck blows and the fine is doubled upon him."" No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Suwayd."
"529","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, he said: Abu al-Hudhayl al-Raba'i narrated to me, he said: Abu Dawud took my hand and said: al-Bara ibn Azib took my hand and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: ""There are no two believers who meet and each takes the hand of his companion, taking it only out of love for Allah, then part, except that they are forgiven."""
"530","And with it: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that Bushayr ibn Yasar informed him, that Husayn ibn Mihsan informed him, from his aunt, that she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to her: ""Are you married?"" She said: Yes. He said: ""How are you to him?"" She said: I do not fall short except what I am unable to do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""See where you are from him, for he is your Paradise and your Fire."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq."
"531","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dahir al-Razi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: I heard Hudhayfah say: Whoever is pleased to look at the most similar of people in guidance, conduct and private converse to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he leaves his house until he returns, let him look at Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, except Dahir al-Razi."
"532","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Maryam, he said: Ammar ibn Yasir said: Your mother has come to Basrah, and she is the wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this world, and his wife in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"533","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Labid, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A woman entered the Fire over a cat she tied; she did not give it water, did not feed it, and did not let it eat from the vermin of the earth until it died in its bonds. And a prostitute entered Paradise when she passed a dog at a well wanting water but unable to reach it; so she removed her shoe or boot, tied it in her veil, drew water for it and gave it drink until it was quenched."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Labid except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"534","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle narrated to us, they said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has fought, and whoever looks after him in his family with good has fought."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, except Rawwad."
"535","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid and Mujalid, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he rose for his need wearing a Roman cloak, wiped, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not remove them? He said: ""I put them on in purity."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid and Mujalid except Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad; Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban is alone in transmitting it."
"536","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Hamzah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, the thief does not steal while he is a believer when he steals, and the drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it."" We said: O Messenger of Allah, how is that? He said: ""Faith leaves him; if he repents, it returns to him."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except Ibn Abi Layla; his son is alone in transmitting it from him."
"537","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: Nothing of the world pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor did anything please him of it except piety. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"538","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, says: I do not regard the right of My servant until My servant regards My right."" This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Sallam al-Tawil is alone in transmitting it."
"539","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Fadl al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves the first row fearing to harm anyone, Allah doubles for him the reward of the first row."" This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; al-Walid ibn al-Fadl is alone in transmitting it."
"540","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Shabib al-Muktib narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth and sniff water, and the ears are part of the head."" No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ismail; Ali ibn Hashim is alone in transmitting it."
"541","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to me, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: ""How will you be when a quarter of Paradise is yours, and three quarters for the rest of people?"" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""How will you be when half is yours?"" They said: That is more. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; for you are eighty rows of them."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman except al-Harith; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad is alone in transmitting it."
"542","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: He married her while unlawful, and consummated with her while lawful; then she died at Sarif, and that is her grave beneath the shed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Dinar except Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq."
"543","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Abbadani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali narrate, from his father, he said: I fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Hunayn in year eight in Ramadan; it coincided with a rainy Friday, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called: Prayer in the dwellings. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Mu'awiyah al-Abbadani except Ali ibn al-Ja'd."
"544","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar ibn Yasir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Tayammum is one strike for the face and the hands."" No one narrated this hadith from Aban except Affan."
"545","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to me, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Tawus narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Beware of arrogance, for arrogance is in a man even if he wears a cloak."" No one narrated this hadith from Tawus except Abdullah ibn Humayd; Suwayd is alone in transmitting it."
"546","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Suwayd narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi, that the Messenger of Allah ordered him to announce among the people of Mina in two cloaks: No one shall fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking."
"547","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle narrated to us, they said: Suwayd narrated to us, from Qurrah, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Menstruation came upon me while I was with the Messenger of Allah on his bed; so I slipped away until I fell to the ground. He said: ""What is the matter with you?"" I told him I had menstruated, so he ordered me to tie my waist-wrapper to the middle of my thighs and return."
"548","And from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the prayer."""
"549","And from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever among you comes to Friday, let him wash."""
"550","And from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Aflah ibn Abi al-Qu'ays asked permission to enter upon her, and she said: Until I ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I asked him, and he said: ""Let him enter upon you, for he is your uncle."" And he said: ""What is unlawful by lineage is unlawful by suckling."""
"551","And from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while she lay across in front of him on the bed."
"552","And from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about a man who breaks his ablution in prayer. He said: ""He shall not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."""
"553","And from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I came on a donkey, having nearly reached puberty, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with the people; I passed part of the row, then let it loose, returned, then prayed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not repeat anything to me."
"554","And from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted in the year of the Conquest until he reached al-Kadid, then broke fast, and his companions broke fast; they follow the latest of the Messenger of Allah's commands, and that is the abrogating, decisive one."
"555","And from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When you see the crescent, fast; when you see it, break fast; if it is obscured to you, complete thirty."" No one narrated these hadiths from Qurrah except Suwayd and Rushdayn."
"556","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat; whoever witnesses it until it is buried has two qirats; and whoever eats of this herb shall not approach our mosque."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Jarir."
"557","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Mujahid, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: What do you say about Ali? He said: That is his house. He said: What do you say about Uthman? He said: ""What shall I say about a man who committed a sin between him and Allah, and He pardoned him, and committed a sin between you and him, and you killed him."" No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Yazid ibn Mihran is alone in transmitting it."
"558","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salamah al-Aftas narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to the desert becomes harsh; whoever follows game becomes heedless; and whoever comes to the ruler is tempted."" No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Ayyub ibn Musa, except Abdullah ibn Salamah; al-Qawariri is alone in transmitting it. Abu Nu'aym and others narrated it from Sufyan, from Abu Musa al-Yamani."
"559","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever raises two girls until they mature, I and he will enter Paradise"" - and he pointed with his two fingers, the thumb and the one next to it. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"560","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, they said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Seven are from the Sunnah for the boy on the seventh day: he is named, circumcised, harm is removed from him, his ear is pierced, an aqiqah is offered for him, his head is shaved, it is smeared with the blood of his aqiqah, and charity is given of the weight of the hair of his head in gold or silver. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Rawwad."
"561","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nadabah narrated to us, he said: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik wearing a red fur, and he said: Our blankets in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - we would wear them and pray in them. No one narrated this hadith from Rashid except al-Hasan ibn Habib."
"562","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Ubayd al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Hakim al-Habati narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating; Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered him to take her back; if it seemed to him, he would divorce her while she is pure at the start of her waiting period."
"563","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever claims lineage to other than his father, or takes as masters other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people."" No one narrated this hadith except Wuhayb, from Ibn Khuthaym."
"564","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Isa al-Qanadili narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Zayd and Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no morning or evening but that the regions of the earth call to one another: O neighbor, did a righteous servant pass by you today who prayed upon you or remembered Allah? If it says: Yes, it sees for it thereby a merit over it."" This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Salih al-Murri is alone in transmitting it."
"565","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrate, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Corner will come on the Day of Resurrection greater than Abu Qubays, with a tongue and two lips, testifying for whoever touched it in truth; and it is the right hand of Allah, mighty and majestic, with which He shakes the hands of His creation."" No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Abdullah ibn Amr, except Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal."
"566","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Qays, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have left no trial after me more harmful to men than women."""
"567","And from al-Mughirah ibn Qays, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman will not be straight for you upon one character; she is only like a rib: if you straighten it you break it, and if you leave it you enjoy it while crookedness is in it."""
"568","And from al-Mughirah ibn Qays, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the dawn in the mosque, with believing women behind him; when he gave salam, they would go out in their wraps, unrecognized due to the darkness."
"569","And from al-Mughirah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I was given the strength of forty in might and intercourse, and no believer but is given the strength of ten; and desire was made in ten parts, nine parts of it placed in women and one in men; were it not for the modesty cast upon them with their desires, each man would have nine ardent women."""
"570","And from al-Mughirah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, but let them not come except unscented."""
"571","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a day's journey except with a husband or a mahram."""
"572","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle narrated to us, they said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan and al-Mughirah ibn Qays narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Ajfa al-Sulami, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he said: O people, do not be extravagant in the dowries of women; had it been an honor with people or piety with Allah, the most deserving of that would have been the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he did not marry any of his wives, nor marry off any of his daughters, except for twelve ounces and a nashsh. One of you is extravagant in a woman's dowry until he says: Did I not burden you with the strap of the waterskin? He said: I was a young boy, so I did not know what the strap of the waterskin is. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Mughirah except Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"573","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, they said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi al-Abbas, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Jews used to say: When a man comes to his wife from behind in her vulva, his child will be cross-eyed. So Allah, exalted, revealed: ""Your women are a tillage for you."""
"574","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah al-Makhzumi, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What will be opened for my community after me was shown to me, and it pleased me."" So Allah, exalted, revealed: ""And the Hereafter is better for you than the first"" to His saying: ""And you shall be pleased"" - Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces of pearl, their soil musk, in each palace what befits him."
"575","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Marwan narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger"" - he said: They are from Ukl. No one narrated these hadiths from Mu'awiyah except Marwan."
"576","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever's last words are: There is no god but Allah, shall not enter the Fire."" No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Abu al-Ahwas."
"577","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Abbad, he said: I said to Ali: Tell me about this march of yours: is it a pledge pledged to you by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or an opinion you held? No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ibn Ulayyah."
"578","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Abbad, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Madinah and said: ""Allah has purified the people of this city, so long as the stars do not lead them astray."" No one narrated this hadith from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Abbad, except Qays ibn al-Rabi'; Abu Bilal is alone in transmitting it. Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi and al-Hasan ibn Atiyah narrated it from Qays, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"579","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd and Qays ibn Sa'd, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the night prayer one night until the people slept, then woke; Umar came and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah. So he came out and prayed with them, and he did not mention that they performed ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hammad; Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib and Ibn Aishah are alone in transmitting it."
"580","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Madini narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever sees one favored over him in wealth and creation, let him look to one below him."" No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr except his son Sa'id; Abdullah ibn Ja'far is alone in transmitting it."
"581","579 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: When Abu Lu'lu'ah stabbed Umar, he stabbed him twice, and Umar thought he had some offense against the people that he did not know of, so he called Ibn Abbas - and he loved him, kept him close, and listened to him - and said to him: I would like you to find out whether this came from a group of the people. So Ibn Abbas went out, and he did not pass by any group of people except that they were weeping, then he returned to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I did not come upon any group of Muslims except that they were weeping, as if today they had lost their firstborn children. He said: Who killed me? He said: Abu Lu'lu'ah the Magian, the slave of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. Ibn Abbas said: So I saw joy on his face. He said: Praise be to Allah who did not afflict me through the word of anyone who would argue against me with the word 'there is no god but Allah.' Indeed I had forbidden you from bringing any of the foreign captives to us, but you disobeyed me. Then he said: Call my brothers to me. They said: And who? He said: Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. So they sent for them, then he placed his head in my lap, and when they came I said: These have arrived. He said: Yes, I have considered the affair of the Muslims and found you, O six, to be the heads of the people and their leaders, and this matter will only be among you; as long as you remain upright the affair of the people will remain upright, and if there is disagreement it will be among you. When I heard mention of disagreement and division I thought it would happen, for seldom did he say anything except that I saw it. Then the blood flowed heavily, and they whispered among themselves until I feared they would pledge allegiance to one of them, so I said: The Commander of the Faithful is still alive, and there cannot be two caliphs with one looking at the other. He said: Carry me, so we carried him, and he said: Consult for three days, and Suhayb will lead the people in prayer. He said: Whom shall we consult, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: Consult the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and the chiefs of the armies here. Then he asked for a drink of milk, and drank, and the whiteness of the milk came out of the two wounds, so it was known that it was death, and he said: Now, if I had the whole world I would ransom myself with it from the terror of the ascent, though - and praise be to Allah - I have seen nothing but good. Ibn Abbas said: Even if you say that, may Allah reward you with good; did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate that Allah strengthen the religion and the Muslims through you when they were fearful in Makkah, and when you accepted Islam your Islam was a source of might, and Islam became manifest through you along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, and you migrated to Madinah and your migration was a victory, then you were not absent from any battlefield witnessed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in fighting the polytheists, on such-and-such day and such-and-such day, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while he was pleased with you, and you supported the caliph after him upon the way of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), striking those who turned away with those who came forward until people entered Islam willingly or unwillingly, then the caliph passed away while he was pleased with you, then you were appointed with the best appointment of the people: Allah founded cities through you, collected revenues through you, repelled the enemy through you, and Allah brought through you to every household an expansion in their religion and an expansion in their provisions, then He sealed for you with martyrdom, so congratulations to you. He said: By Allah, indeed the deceived one is the one whom you deceive. Then he said: Will you testify for me, O Abdullah, before Allah on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Yes. He said: O Allah, to You belongs praise. Put my cheek on the ground, O Abdullah ibn Umar - so I moved it from my thigh to my leg. He said: Put my cheek on the ground, so he left his beard and cheek until they fell to the ground, and said: Woe to you and woe to your mother, O Umar, if Allah does not forgive you. Then he passed away, may Allah have mercy on him. When he passed away they sent to Abdullah ibn Umar, and he said: I will not come to you unless you do what he commanded you of consulting the Muhajirun and the Ansar and the chiefs of the armies here. Al-Hasan said - and Umar's conduct at his death and his fear of his Lord were mentioned to him - he said: This is how the believer is: he combines good deeds with compassion, while the hypocrite combines evil deeds with delusion. By Allah, I have not found, in what has passed nor in what remains, a servant who increased in good deeds except that he increased in fear and compassion from Him, nor have I found, in what has passed nor in what remains, a servant who increased in evil deeds except that he increased in delusion. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"582","580 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, the brother of Abu Ma'mar, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Glorifying Allah in the prayer is for men, and clapping is for women."
"583","581 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Khidash al-Muhallabi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me from selling what I do not have. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Khalid ibn Khidash."
"584","582 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from A'ishah, who said: When what the people of the slander said reached me, I intended to go to a well and throw myself into it. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Zayd; Khalid ibn Khidash is alone in transmitting it."
"585","583 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Salih al-Nahhas narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah Almighty said: Whomever I deprive of his two beloved ones and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bishr except Hushaym, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"586","584 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us: my uncle Isa ibn Musawir narrated to me, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Asadi, from Asma' ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: When a man narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would make him swear an oath, and when he swore I would believe him, and Abu Bakr narrated to me - and Abu Bakr spoke the truth - that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who commits a sin, then prays two rak'ahs, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi al-Abbas except Marwan; Isa ibn al-Musawir is alone in transmitting it."
"587","585 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Jarir who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakat, and give sincere advice to every Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Isma'il ibn Zakariyya; Sa'id ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it."
"588","586 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle Isa narrated to us, they said: Suwayd narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it without asking you will be helped in it, and if you are given it after asking you will be left to it; and when you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate for your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Suwayd; the two sons of al-Musawir are alone in transmitting it."
"589","587 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the statement of Allah Almighty: Whatever you cut down of date-palms or left standing on their roots, it was by Allah's permission - he said: al-linah is the date-palm. And that He may disgrace the disobedient - he said: They brought them down from their fortresses, and they were commanded to cut the palms, and it weighed on their hearts, so the Muslims said: We cut some of it and left some of it, so we will ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there reward for us in what we cut, and is there sin upon us in what we left? So Allah Almighty revealed: Whatever you cut down of date-palms or left standing on their roots, it was by Allah's permission, and that He may disgrace the disobedient. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Amrah except Hafs; Affan is alone in transmitting it."
"590","588 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not sit at a table over which wine is passed around. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except al-Hasan."
"591","589 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ismah al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Majza'ah ibn Zahir, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting Ashura, and said: Whoever is fasting should complete his fast, and whoever is not fasting should complete the rest of his day. No one narrated this hadith from Majza'ah except Sharik."
"592","590 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Abdullah ibn Shikhkhir narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Ishaq ibn Isa ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas in his house, and he narrated to us from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas who said: Abu Bakr had a sitting place with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he would not vacate except for al-Abbas, and that used to please the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day al-Abbas came, and Abu Bakr moved from his sitting place for him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, your uncle has come. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him, then turned to Abu Bakr smiling and said: This is al-Abbas who has come wearing white garments, and his children after him will wear black, and twelve men among them will rule. When al-Abbas came he said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you say to Abu Bakr? He said: I said nothing but good. He said: You spoke the truth, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, you say nothing but good. He said: I said: My uncle has come wearing white garments, and his children after him will wear black, and twelve men among them will rule. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq except Hafs; Muhammad ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"593","591 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: my uncle Isa ibn al-Musawir narrated to me, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning on a trunk, and when the pulpit was built the trunk moaned, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced it and it became still. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except al-Walid ibn Muslim; Isa ibn al-Musawir is alone in transmitting it."
"594","592 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that rain was withheld during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah until prices rose, and they feared destruction for their wealth, and we feared destruction for ourselves, so we said: Supplicate your Lord to give us rain. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands to the sky - and by Allah, we did not see any whiteness in the sky - and by Allah, he did not lower his hands until I saw the sky splitting from here and there, until I saw piled clouds, and it poured for seven nights and their days, from one Friday to the next Friday, with the sky pouring down. They said: We fear drowning, so supplicate your Lord for us to withhold it. So I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands, while we did not see any greenery in the sky, and he said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: By Allah, he did not lower his hands until I saw the sky break open. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak, from al-Hasan and Thabit together, except Sa'id ibn Sulayman."
"595","593 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The month is twenty-nine days; when you see the crescent fast, and when you see it break the fast, and if it is obscured from you then estimate for it. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn al-Fadl except Abu Bilal."
"596","594 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh kept restraining themselves from me until Abu Talib died. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Qays; Abu Bilal is alone in transmitting it."
"597","595 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The most beloved supplication to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was to supplicate three times. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, except Za'idah; Husayn is alone in transmitting it. And the companions of Abu Ishaq narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah."
"598","596 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, the brother of Abu Ma'mar, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the testimony of the midwife. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik."
"599","597 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Isma'il ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi who said: When al-Husayn ibn Ali intended to go out to Iraq, Ibn Umar said to him: Do not go out, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the choice between this world and the Hereafter and chose the Hereafter, and you will never attain it, nor anyone of your children. When he refused except to go out, Ibn Umar said to him: I entrust you to Allah as one to be killed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Yahya ibn Isma'il ibn Salim, and no one narrated it from Yahya ibn Isma'il except Sa'id ibn Sulayman and Shababab ibn Sawwar."
"600","598 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Muslim, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves against people with suspicion. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Baqiyyah is alone in transmitting it."
